Team Results

Team Standings

Related News', '2019-09-13', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Results and Scores from Week 2 - 2019', 'results-and-scores-from-week-2-2019', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Defending champs Bugle off to a great start after week 2 more Defending champs Bugle A took all 5 frames off there B team to jump to the top of the Victory League with only George Lory close to gaining a frame for…', null, null, 'Defending champs Bugle off to a great start after week 2 more Defending champs Bugle A took all 5 frames off there B team to jump to the top of the Victory League with only George Lory close to gaining a frame for the second string Matt Mills and Mark Ashton took 2 good points for Meva A at Treggy A who had Rich Pearson to thank as he beat Predator Tregale in the final frame to seal the win Bethel A got a 4 1 victory at Meva D which could of easily been the other way round as the home team suffered late on in the first 4 frames Andy Ridgemans 51 break was the highlight as St Neot got 4 points at Bethel D with Jason Pascoe unlucky to lose out to Darren Lock on a respotted black Meva B have made a great start to the campaign beating Treggy B 4 1 with Phil Hooley gaining the solitary point for the visitors In the Rees league Treggy D go top after getting all the frames at Lerryn and look strong enough to maintain a challenge Amanda Fleming Steve Strickland and Natalie Rosevear were Treggy Cs heroes as they beat Gorran 3 2 who replied through Lee Mckinstry and Rob Bunney St Blazey went 3 up at Bugle C but were pegged back by Mo Roscorla and Phil Johns and in the Bethel derby the B team grabbed bragging rights as Wayne Jordan Jim Tamblyn and Clive Stuthridge won there 3 frames with Roger Smithson and Leigh Rosevear pulling 2 back for the C team', '2019-09-20', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Results and Scores from Week 3 – 2019', 'results-and-scores-from-week-3-2019', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Bugle A make big statement in there title defence as they beat Treggy A 4-1 more Andrew Bests 46 and Barrie Mcintoshs 57 the 2 standout moments of the night. St Neot move into second place after grabbing all 5 frames…', null, null, 'Bugle A make big statement in there title defence as they beat Treggy A 4-1 more Andrew Bests 46 and Barrie Mcintoshs 57 the 2 standout moments of the night. St Neot move into second place after grabbing all 5 frames off Meva D as Andy Ridgeman continued his break a week run with a fine 49. Meva A got there first win of the season taking all 5 frames off there B team as James Popplewell knocked in a 32 and Mark Ashton a 44. Pelynt got a good 4 1 home win against Bethel D who got there single point as Gavin Dyche defeated Andy Parnell and Treggy B got there first win as they defeated Bugle B whose only point came courtesy of Keith Moore. In the Rees League Treggy D have a 5 point lead after beating St Blazey 4 1 with only Stewart Dewings stemming the flow when defeating Ryan Taylor as Graham Taylor Mark Sullivan Liam Reynolds and Keiron Clemes secured wins for the table toppers. Bugle C got there first win as Mo Roscorla Phil Johns and Roy Bayliss prevailed verses Treggy C who replied through Caz Stephens and Steve Strickland. In a game pulled forward a few nights Meva C got the better of Lostwithiel by the odd frame as Predator Tregale Darren Elliott and Pete Chambers won with Craig Nicholls and Darren Biggen replying.', '2019-09-26', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Results and Scores from Week 4 – 2019', 'results-and-scores-from-week-4-2019', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Bugle A stay clear at the top of the Victory League more Bugle A took 4 points at Treggy B with Phil Hooley seeing off Ian Ball for the home side with Andrew Gooch narrowing missing out to Jake Moore Colin Rundle and…', null, null, 'Bugle A stay clear at the top of the Victory League more Bugle A took 4 points at Treggy B with Phil Hooley seeing off Ian Ball for the home side with Andrew Gooch narrowing missing out to Jake Moore Colin Rundle and Keith Moore put Bugle B 2 up at home to Meva A but the tide turned as Matt Chesterfield Paul Williams (33 break)and Matt Mills (32) completed the turnaround Ben Prynn took out Rich Pearson to give Meva D a great start at home to Treggy A but Barrie Mcintosh(42) Chris Stephenson Jason Cocks and Martin Knight secured the win to keep them in 2nd Jason Hills (38) and Dave Grose put Pelynt 2 up at Bethel A only for Geoff Hawken and Bob Stephens to level things up but the away side got the win as Phil Ormond defeated Garry Stephens Treggy D got a good 4 1 home victory against Bugle C to stay top of the Rees League with Roy Bayliss getting the away point defeating Steve Knight Big movers of the week were Bethel C after taking all 5 points off Meva C to go joint second Lostwithiel and Treggy C fought a close match all evening with the home side sneaking through 3 2 as Darren Biggen Terry Nicholls and John Wilton winning with Shaun Strickland and Victoria Rollings replying St Blazey beat Gorran 3 2 as Billy Vigus Mike Delaney and Stewy Dewings were victorious with the reliable Lee Mckinstry and Rob Bunney winners for the visitors', '2019-10-09', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Results and Scores from Week 5 – 2019', 'results-and-scores-from-week-5-2019', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Meva B trounce Pelynt on there own turf more Mevagissey B produced the performance of the week as they trounced Pelynt 4 1 on there own turf with Pete Chambers 47 and 50 breaks the standout as he thrashed John…', null, null, 'Meva B trounce Pelynt on there own turf more Mevagissey B produced the performance of the week as they trounced Pelynt 4 1 on there own turf with Pete Chambers 47 and 50 breaks the standout as he thrashed John Daniell 115 to 1. Dave Grose got the home point beating Mark Gregory on the black Bugle A took all 5 at home to Meva D to be well clear at the top but Paul Sturtridge and Ian Ball were pushed all the way by Scott Mills and Ian Latham respectively Meva A jump to second place after defeating Treggy B 4 1 in comfortable fashion with Phil Hooleys defeat of Matt Chesterfield stopping the whitewash Bethel D will be rueing missed chances after dipping out to Bugle B by the odd frame as both searched for there first win Jason Pascoe and Gavin Dyche took the home points with Mike Williams George Lory and Keith Moore replying Father and son Graham and Ryan Taylor both won along with Kieron Clemes and Mark Sullivan as leaders Tregonissey D claimed a good win at Gorran who replied through Lee Mckinstry Bethel C are looking good after taking all 5 frames at Treggy C and have a game in hand on the leaders Bugle C got a fine 4 1 home win over Lostwithiel to climb the table with wins for Roy Bayliss Damien Knight Kev Spencer and Nige Couchman with Craig Nicholls replying Lerryns first win of the season came at Bethel B when taking 4 points to move off the bottom of the table as Terry Middleton Matt Woodward John Hancock and the fit again Graham Hoskin won with Clive Stuthridge beating the unlucky Charles Mcmiram in the final frame of the evening', '2019-10-09', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Competitions - Round 1', 'competitions-round-1', 'Competitions', '[]'::jsonb, 'St Blazey caused the biggest shock in the team handicap as they despatched top flight Bethel A 3 0 more Mickey Meares superb 22 clearance to beat Leon Collard the standout memory of the evening. James Popplewell…', null, null, 'St Blazey caused the biggest shock in the team handicap as they despatched top flight Bethel A 3 0 more Mickey Meares superb 22 clearance to beat Leon Collard the standout memory of the evening. James Popplewell excellent 63 break saw Meva A home against there D team and Lerryn took the first 3 frames at Gorran to procede Darren Biggens last frame victory against Josh Bristow saw Lostwithiel progress at the expense of Bethel B Bethel C came from 2 down at home to Treggy B to win whilst Bugle A showed there class despatching Treggy D 3 0 as did Meva B who took out Treggy C by the same score The first 4 frames were shared at Pelynt leaving John Daniells defeat of Mike Williams of Bugle B to decide the tie and Meva C pushed Treggy A all the way but dipped out 3 1 In a rearranged Victory League game Bethel D had an excellent 4 1 win at Meva B to move them up 3 places in the league', '2019-10-18', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Results and Scores from Week 6 – 2019', 'results-and-scores-from-week-6-2019', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'A night of big breaks at Bethel more With Ryan Bilsons 54 Barrie Mcintoshs 50 Garry Stephens 37 but lost the frame to Jason Cocks 42 as Treggy A secured a 3 2 win to move them up to second in the Victory League St…', null, null, 'A night of big breaks at Bethel more With Ryan Bilsons 54 Barrie Mcintoshs 50 Garry Stephens 37 but lost the frame to Jason Cocks 42 as Treggy A secured a 3 2 win to move them up to second in the Victory League St Neots good run continued as they came away from Meva B with 4 frames. Darren Lock knocked in a 44 with Dave Kendall lowering Anthony Maddams flag to get the home point Bugle Bs troubles carry on as they were whitewashed on there own table by Pelynt who join Treggy A in joint second in the table and Bethel D picked up a vital win at Treggy B with victories for Dale and Gavin Dyche and Rich Wilkinson with Andrew Gooch and Phil Hooley registering for the home side Bethel C jumped to the top of the Rees League as they beat Bugle C 5 0 with Courtney Crockfords 22 clearance and potting the re-spotted black the standout moments of the evening Meva C picked up a welcome 3 2 win at Lerryn with Predator Tregale Pete Chambers and Joe Chesterfield there winners with Graham Hoskin and Matt Woodward replying Gorran came away from Lostwithiel after winning by the odd frame as Geoff Hayhurst beat Matt Moore in the final frame Another team to win away was Bethel B at St Blazey as Wayne Jordan Clive Stuthridge and Guy Buckle won with the home team points got through Richie Bolt and Billy Vigus', '2019-10-24', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Results and Scores from Week 7 – 2019', 'results-and-scores-from-week-7-2019', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Bugle A continue there 100% record by sweeping aside Bethel A 4-1 more Gary Spencers fine 60 break the hi-light of the night with Leon Collards defeat of Jake Moore saving the whitewash. Pelynt jumped to second place…', null, null, 'Bugle A continue there 100% record by sweeping aside Bethel A 4-1 more Gary Spencers fine 60 break the hi-light of the night with Leon Collards defeat of Jake Moore saving the whitewash. Pelynt jumped to second place after taking 4 frames at home to Treggy B who had newlywed Justin Hooley to thank for there point after beating John Daniell with Jason Hill knocking in a 30. St Neot got 4 points at home to Bugle B to sit joint third with Darren Locks 31 being equalled by Colin Rundle in his defeat to Chris Perring. James Tomlinsons 42 break helped basement boys Meva D pick up 2 welcome points at Bethel D with Rich Lakemans defeat of Ross Mcmenemy securing there other frame Whilst Meva B took 2 good points at Treggy A with wins for Dave Kendall over Chris Stephenson backed up by Mark Gregorys win against Martin Knight Barry Mac knocked in a 39 break. Leaders of the Rees Bethel C went 2 down at Gorran after wins for Lee Mckinstry and Rob Bunney but they managed to win the last 3 to stay 3 points clear of the chasing pack. Bethel B had a great win over Treggy D also coming back from 2 down as Wayne Jordan Jim Tamblyn and Clive Stuthridge took there frames to move up to joint 5th. Amanda Fleming got Treggy C off to a winning start against Lerryns John Hancock but that was as good as it got as Charles Mcmiram Terry Middleton Graham Hoskin and Matt Woodward sealed an excellent win. St Blazey got 4 points at struggling Meva C with Darren Elliotts black ball win over Billy Vigus saving the whitewash.', '2019-10-30', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Results and Scores from Week 8 – 2019', 'results-and-scores-from-week-8-2019', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Bugle march to 7 points clear at the top of the Victory League more After taking all 5 frames at Mevagissey B and now 7 points clear at the top of the Victory League Bugle A are going to take some stopping with Jake…', null, null, 'Bugle march to 7 points clear at the top of the Victory League more After taking all 5 frames at Mevagissey B and now 7 points clear at the top of the Victory League Bugle A are going to take some stopping with Jake Moores blackball win over Matt Rowe helping secure the whitewash Pelynts fine form continues with a 4 1 win at Meva D Ben Prynns win against Andy Parnell stopping the nap hand Treggy B scored a excellent 3 2 home win against St Neot with wins for Andrew Gooch Stuart Giles and Phil Hooley with Darren Lock getting a 37 break in reply Barrie Mcintosh hit a fine 40 break to help Treggy A win 4 1 at Bugle B with Colin Rundle defeating Jason Cocks for the home point In a rearranged game on Monday Bethel A got a great 4 1 at St Neot with Matt Green giving Darren Lock a rare defeat St Blazey moved up to second place in the Rees League after betting Treggy C 4 1 with Amanda Fleming taking out Billy Vigus for the visitors point Lerryn continue to climb the table and raced into a 3 0 lead at home to Bugle through Woodward Hoskin and Middleton only for Kev Spencer and Nige Couchman to take the final 2 frames Bethel B got 3 points at Lostwithiel through Josh Bristow Wayne Jordan and Jim Tamblyn with Darren Biggen and Matt Moore replying', '2019-11-10', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Results and Scores from Week 9 – 2019', 'results-and-scores-from-week-9-2019', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Rees league title up for grabs for multiple teams this year more It''s any ones guess who will win the Rees League this year as previous leaders Bethel C were beaten 4-1 at home to St Blazey who take over at the top…', null, null, 'Rees league title up for grabs for multiple teams this year more It''s any ones guess who will win the Rees League this year as previous leaders Bethel C were beaten 4-1 at home to St Blazey who take over at the top It was Leigh Rosevears 18 clearance in the final frame against Stewart Dewings that stopped the whitewash and who knows how the table will look at the half way stage Bethel B move in to the promotion frame after a 4 1 win at Bugle C with Mo Roscorlas defeat of Josh Bristow stopping the nap hand Mevagissey C picked up a welcome win at Gorran by the odd frame with Joe Chesterfields win over Geoff Hayhurst sealing the victory And Lerryn keep rising the table with another good win this time at Lostwithiel Graham Hoskin Matt Woodward and Terry Middleton were there marksmen In the Victory League Bugle A continue to rack up the points and it was only Dave Grose who stopped a whitewash over Pelynt by defeating Ian Ball Barrie Mcintoshs 45 and Ryan Bilsons 34 helped Treggy A to a 4 1 win against Bethel D with Gavin Dyche taking out Jason Cocks for the away point Meva D got there first win by defeating there B team by the odd frame as Ian Latham took out Natham Shaw in the decider Whilst in the room next door Matt Mills defeat of Darren Lock helped Meva A to a good win over St Neot who have slipped of late and even Matt Vesseys 30 break not enough to beat Mark Ashton Chairman Garry Stephens 48 break and win for Matt Green and Leon Collard put Bethel A in a great position against Treggy B who fought back with a faultless performance by Stuart Giles and a event full frame win for Andrew Gooch over Geoff Hawken', '2019-11-14', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Competitions', 'competitions', 'Competitions', '[]'::jsonb, 'Team pairs Quarter finals results more It was quarter final of the team pairs on tuesday with 4 away wins. Bugle A went to Mevagissey A and took the first 4 games to progress Bethel A also got a 4 0 win at…', null, null, 'Team pairs Quarter finals results more It was quarter final of the team pairs on tuesday with 4 away wins. Bugle A went to Mevagissey A and took the first 4 games to progress Bethel A also got a 4 0 win at Tregonissey C although Amanda Fleming and Caz Stephens were very unlucky to lose out to Leon Collard and Garry Stephens in the second frame Tregonissey A dropped the first frame to St Blazeys Pete Bate and Mark Cockayne but recovered to take the next 4 frames whilst St Neot went 3 up at Bethel D only for the hosts to pull back the next 2 frames but had a points deficit proved to much for them to overcome especially after Darren Locks 55 break put the tie beyond reach In a preliminary Team Plate game Lee Mckinstry and Steve Williams put Gorran 2 up at Mevagissey C only for the hosts to level up through Joe Chesterfield and David Tregale leaving Mark Wherrys defeat of Adrian Evans to send Gorran on to an away tie at Bugle C on 10th December', '2019-11-21', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Results and Scores from Week 10 – 2019', 'results-and-scores-from-week-10-2019', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Mevagissey A on fire as big breaks help them to 3rd in the Victory League more Mevagissey D produced a great 5-0 home win over Bugle B to move off the bottom of the table and give themselves a great chance of staying…', null, null, 'Mevagissey A on fire as big breaks help them to 3rd in the Victory League more Mevagissey D produced a great 5-0 home win over Bugle B to move off the bottom of the table and give themselves a great chance of staying up with there opponents replacing them at the foot Bugle A went 2 up at home to St Neot through Gary Spencer and Andrew Best but wins for Matt Vessey Steve Courts and Darren Lock inflicted Bugle s first defeat and also lost the Runabout Shield Meva A are really on fire as Paul Williams 33 Mark Ashtons 37 and James Popplewells 42 helped them beat Bethel D 4 1 Matt Mills there other winner with Dayle Dyche with the away point Rich Broad and Dave Grose put Pelynt 2 up at Treggy A who bounced back to win through Martin Knight Barrie Mcintosh and Ryan Bilson to remain second Meva B played well at Bethel A but only had Mark Gregorys win against Leon Collard to show for it as messers Hawken Peers Green and Stephens took the home points The Rees League is very tight with 3 points separating the top 3 sides Bethel C took out Treggy D by the odd frame to lead the table Ben Stunnel and Howard Brett both won on the black to win the first 2 frames but Mark Sullivan and Graham Taylor levelled things up leaving Martin Powells defeat of Ryan Taylor to seal the win St Blazey moved closer with a good 4 1 victory at Lostwithiel with Mike Delaney knocking in a 31 break against John Wilton with Terry Nicholls beating Stewart Dewings for the home side Caz Stephens and James Beeches put Treggy C 2 up at home to Bethel B but comfortable wins for Jim Tamblyn Wayne Jordan and Clive Stuthridge completed the comeback Bugle C and Meva C played out 5 really tight frames with Meva going 3 up before Phil Johns and Kev Spencer pulled the last 2 frames back', '2019-12-08', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Team Handicap', 'team-handicap', 'Competitions', '[]'::jsonb, 'Team handicap games are always a great leveller but Bugle A escaped a potential banana skin at Lostwithiel coming through 3-0. more Pelynt got a great 3 1 win at Mevagissey A with wins for Phil Ormond Jason Hill and…', null, null, 'Team handicap games are always a great leveller but Bugle A escaped a potential banana skin at Lostwithiel coming through 3-0. more Pelynt got a great 3 1 win at Mevagissey A with wins for Phil Ormond Jason Hill and Richard Broad with Paul Williams getting the home point knocking in a 36 break. In the adjoining room Meva B got the first 3 frames to see off Bethel C with all looking close games In the Plate competition Treggy C went 2 up over there D team after victories for Lynn Kearns and Caz Stephens but couldn''t hold on as Mark Sullivan Keiron Clemes and Graham Taylor sealed the win. Gorran are looking to go farther than last years semi final place and progressed at the expense of Bugle C 3 1 Bethel B took the first frame against there A team as Clive Stuthridge took out Garry Stephens but wins for Bob Stephens Matt Greens blackball win over Guy Buckle and Leon Collards comprehensive victory over Jim Tamblyn saw the A team home, whilst Bugle B came from 2 down to beat Treggy B with Mike Williams win over Andrew Gooch sealing the excellent win', '2019-12-13', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Results and Scores from Week 11 – 2019', 'results-and-scores-from-week-11-2019', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Second placed Mevagissey A did there utmost to close the gap on leaders Bugle A more As Paul Williams and James Popplewell both knocked in 33 breaks in there victories but Paul Sturtridge Andrew Best and Gary Spencer…', null, null, 'Second placed Mevagissey A did there utmost to close the gap on leaders Bugle A more As Paul Williams and James Popplewell both knocked in 33 breaks in there victories but Paul Sturtridge Andrew Best and Gary Spencer sealed the win for the tabletoppers who hold a 8 point buffer In the Tregonissey derby the A team took the honours with a single frame win against there B team who got there points through Stuart Giles and Andrew Gooch who gave Barrie Mcintosh his first defeat as he knocked in a fine 39 Jason Hill had a 30 break against Chris Perring but lost the frame as St Neot returned from Pelynt with a 4 1 victory with Dave Grose beating Matt Vessey to stay unbeaten this season Bugle B got 2 welcome points at Meva B as they bid to get away from the wrong end of the table as Keith Moore and Dave Rundle got wins with Ben Rothwell Nathan Shaw and Dave Kendall replying And Chairman Garry Stephens broke down on a break of 58 when well placed to beat the seasons best of 77 as he sealed a 3 2 win for Bethel A against there D team earlier wins for Geoff Hawken and Andy Peers were cancelled out by Jason Pascoe and Rich Wilkinson to set up the last frame decider In the Rees league Bethel C took all 5 frames at Lostwithiel to open up a 2 point lead at the top Second placed Treggy D got 4 frames off there C team to stay in contention with young Ryan Taylors 33 break the highlight with Vicky Rollings beating Steve Knight to get the C teams point Lerryn got a great single frame win at home to St Blazey with victories for Matt Woodward John Hancock and Terry Middleton with Mark Haley and Richie Bolt replying Lee Mckinstry remains unbeaten helping Gorran Haven to record a win at Bugle C Rob Bunney and Steve Williams also got wins with Mo Roscorla and Nige Couchman winning there games And Bethel B got all 5 frames at home to the luckless Meva C to move in to third place with Clive Stuthridges 33 break the standout action of the evening', '2020-01-09', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Results and Scores from Week 12 – 2019', 'results-and-scores-from-week-12-2019', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'It really is hotting up in the Rees League as leaders Bethel C loose out to there B team more Bugle A whitewashed there B team to move a massive 10 points clear at the top of the Victory League with Gary Spencer…', null, null, 'It really is hotting up in the Rees League as leaders Bethel C loose out to there B team more Bugle A whitewashed there B team to move a massive 10 points clear at the top of the Victory League with Gary Spencer knocking in a 40 break Paul Sturtridge a 30 and Andrew Best with a 34 and a 36 as he defeated Keith Moore Mevagissey A claimed a good 3 2 home win over Tregonissey A to hold on to second place with the visitors back in third Matt Mills having a 36 when beating Rich Pearson with Jason Cocks getting a 31 in beating Matty Chesterfield Ross Mcmenemys win over Ant Maddams was Bethel Ds only success as the were well beaten at St Neot but that point has moved them further away from the bottom as Mevagissey D got nothing at Bethel A despite having a great chance in 3 of the games Mevagissey B got an excellent odd frame win at Tregonissey B with wins for Dave Kendall Mark Gregory and Matt Rowe with Andrew Gooch and Stuart Giles pulling back the last 2 frames for the home side It really is hotting up in the Rees League as leaders Bethel C lost out to there B team by the odd frame leaving them level on points with Tregonissey D who got 4 points off Lerryn Clive Stuthridge had a 37 break for Bethel B who themselves are only 3 points off the top The legend that is Charles Mcmirram was Lerryn solitary winner taking out Ryan Taylor for there single point Bugle C picked up 2 good points at St Blazey as Roy Bayliss beat Stew Dewings and Kev Spencer got the better of Mike Delaney (kev got his bearings wrong earlier in the evening and actually turned up at Bethel to play) Mark Cockayne Richie Bolt and Billy Vigus got Blazeys frames Amanda Fleming beat Geoff Hayhurst in the last frame to claim Tregonissey Ds only point at Gorran whose great season continues with victories for Lee Mckinstry Steve Williams Mark Wheery and Rob Bunney', '2020-01-16', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Results and Scores from Week 13 – 2019', 'results-and-scores-from-week-13-2019', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Breaks galore as Bugle stretch clear at the top of the Victory league more Leaders of the Victory league Bugle A went 3 frames up at Tregonissey A through Andrew Best(36 break) Jake Moore and Gary Spencer(44) but the…', null, null, 'Breaks galore as Bugle stretch clear at the top of the Victory league more Leaders of the Victory league Bugle A went 3 frames up at Tregonissey A through Andrew Best(36 break) Jake Moore and Gary Spencer(44) but the home side pulled the last 2 back with wins for Ryan Bilson and Barrie Mcintosh who knocked in a 41 Mevagissey A took out there B team by the odd frame as James Popplewell Mark Ashton and Paul Williams who had a 39 break with Ben Rothwell defeating Matt Mills and Dave Kendalls win against Matt Chesterfield getting the B teams points Ben Prynn and Scott Mills got Meva D 2 welcome points at home to St Neot who replied through Steve Courts (38) Matt Vessey (31) and Darren Lock whilst Jason Hill opened up the evening knocking in a 34 to give Pelynt a winning start at Bethel D which was increased through Dave Grose and Len Flower but the home side took the last 2 frames with wins for Gavin and Dayle Dyche Bugle B picked up only there 2nd win of the season taking out Treggy B 3 2 Dave Rundle and George Lory traded frames with Andrew Gooch and Phil Hooley leaving Mike Williams defeat of Geoff Merriman to settle the evening In the Rees League John Hancock inflicted Lee Mckinstrys first defeat of the season helping Lerryn defeat Gorran by the odd frame with other wins for Matt Woodward and Graham Hoskin with Steve Williams and Geoff Hayhurst getting the away points Bugle C got a great 4 1 victory at Treggy C through Kev Spencer Roy Bayliss Nige Couchman and Mo Roscorla with Alan Meades taking out Damien Knight for the home teams solitary point Craig Nicholls got Lostwithiels single point at home to Meva C for who Preditor Tregale Darren Elliott Louise Winterburn and Adrian Evans with a walkover secured the victory', '2020-01-24', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Results and Scores from Week 14 – 2020', 'results-and-scores-from-week-14-2019', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Tregonissey B cause upset as they beat leaders Bugle A more Tregonissey B really upset Bugle As applecart as they beat the league leaders by the odd frame Paul Baron, Geoff Merriman and Andrew Gooch won there frames…', null, null, 'Tregonissey B cause upset as they beat leaders Bugle A more Tregonissey B really upset Bugle As applecart as they beat the league leaders by the odd frame Paul Baron, Geoff Merriman and Andrew Gooch won there frames to secure a great victory with Gary Spencer who knocked in a fine 49 break and Andrew Best replying. Second placed Mevagissey A failed to take full advantage of Bugles slip up as they dropped 2 points to Bugle B who are in desperate need of points, Paul Williams Mark Ashton and Matt Chesterfield got Mevas frames with Colin Rundle and Keith Moore taking the away points which moves them off the bottom of the table. Mevagissey D lost all 5 frames at Treggy A with Barrie Mcintosh having a 64 break against Ben Prynn along with victories for Martin Knight Rich Pearson Ryan Bilson and Jason Cocks which moves them right back in the hunt for some silverware. Bethel A tend to struggle at Pelynt so were delighted to get a 3 2 win courtesy of wins for Leon Collard Matt Green who gave Dave Grose his first defeat of the season and Geoff Hawken with Richard Broad and Jason Hill replying. Bethel D got a good win at home to Meva B to move farther away from the relegation zone as Jason Pascoe and Gavin and Dayle Dyche got wins with Nathan Shaw and Matt Rowe taking the visitors frames. Bethel C have opened up a 2 point lead at the top of the Rees league after taking all 5 frames at Meva C and second placed Tregonissey D dropping 2 points at Bugle C with Mo Roscorla handing Mark Sullivan his first defeat of the season in a very low scoring frame Kev Spencer got the home sides other point with Keiron Clemes Steve Knight and Graham Taylor getting Treggys frames. St Blazey got 4 good points at Gorran to jump up to third with Lee Mckinstrys walkover being the only brightspot for the seasiders. Lynn Kearns and Ryan Orchard got 2 points for Treggy C and along with a walkover for Natalie Rosevear saw them secure a win over Lostwithiel who replied through Craig Nicholls and Darren Biggen', '2020-01-29', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Results and Scores from Week 15 – 2020', 'results-and-scores-from-week-15-2020', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Bugle A get lucky as Mevagissey B hand them 3 frames more If ever Mevagissey D get any luck they would be well away from the bottom of the league but as normal they hit bad luck against Bugle A and lost 3 frames…', null, null, 'Bugle A get lucky as Mevagissey B hand them 3 frames more If ever Mevagissey D get any luck they would be well away from the bottom of the league but as normal they hit bad luck against Bugle A and lost 3 frames which they should of won with James Tomlinson the only victor over Ian Ball but the leaders are a healthy 10 points ahead of the chasing pack. Paul williams knocked in a great 51 break against Phil Hooley to seal a 3 2 win for Mevagissey A at Tregonissey B there were also victories for James Popplewell and Matt Mills with Stuart Giles and a walkover for Paul Baron registering the home points Bugle B have given themselves a great chance to climb out of the relegation places with a 4 1 win over Bethel D whose only success came from Gavin Dyche with Keith Moore Mike Williams and Colin and Dave Rundle taking the home wins Pelynt got an excellent 4 1 win at Meva B to stay comfortable in 6th place with Nathan Shaw taking out Len Flower for the home point. Bethel A got a good odd frame win over St Neot as Geoff Hawken Matt Green and Andy Peers secured wins with Steve Courts (32 break) and Matt Vessey replying Ryan Orchards black ball win over Roger Smithson got Treggy C off to a good start at Bethel C who fought back to take the remaining 4 frames to stay top of the Rees League but there lead has been cut to just 1 point as Treggy D got all 5 frames at Gorran to make sure of an exciting run in to the end of the season Bugle C went in to a 3 0 lead at Lostwithiel thanks to Mo Roscorla (walkover) Kev Spencer and Nige Couchman but the home side recovered to take the last 2 through Darren Biggan and Terry Nicholls and Matt Woodward and Graham Hoskin got Lerryns points at home to Bethel C who remain in the promotion picture thanks to victories for Wayne Jordan Clive Stuthridge and Guy Buckle Lynn Kearns and Ryan Orchard got 2 points for Treggy C and along with a walkover for Natalie Rosevear saw them secure a win over Lostwithiel who replied through Craig Nicholls and Darren Biggen', '2020-02-07', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Competitions February 2020', 'competitions-february-2020', 'Competitions', '[]'::jsonb, 'Competitions Results and Schedules - February 2020 more Pelynt pulled off a great 3 2 win over Bugle A to progress to the team handicap final where they will face Tregonissey A who sneaked home against Mevagissey B…', null, null, 'Competitions Results and Schedules - February 2020 more Pelynt pulled off a great 3 2 win over Bugle A to progress to the team handicap final where they will face Tregonissey A who sneaked home against Mevagissey B by the same score Jason Hill and Richard Broad traded frames with Jake Moore and Paul Sturtridge leaving Dave Groses defeat of Gary Spencer to settle the match. Matt Rowe put Meva B ahead at Treggy but Barrie Mcintosh and Ryan Bilson responded only for Nathan Shaw to level things up going into the last with Jason Cocks pipping Mark Gregory for the win. In the plate competition Bugle B played well at Gorran to come away with a 3 0 victory to move into the final where they will play Bethel A who had to pull out all the stops to beat Tregonissey D Keiron Clemes and Steve Knight had put Treggy 2 1 up but great wins for Andy Peers and Matt Green took the last 2 frames to seal the win. Competition draws Bill Toms Josh Bristow v Steve Courts Paul Sturtridge v Andy Peers Gary Spencer v Barrie Mcintosh James Popplewell v Graham Taylor Contact by 14 Feb play by 1st March Singles Barrie Mcintosh v Andrew Best Darren Lock v Gavin Dyche contact by 21st Feb play by 5th March Seniors Roger Smithson v Richard Opie John Daniell v Bob Stephens contact by 21st Feb play by 5TH March Willie Thomas Mark Sullivan or Keiran Clemes v Aiden Craddock Wayne Jordan v Richard Bolt Pairs Handicap Mcintosh/Bilson v Best/ Spencer Jordan/Bristow v Hawken/Peers', '2020-02-14', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Results and Scores from Week 16 – 2020', 'results-and-scores-from-week-16-2020', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Race for 2nd hots up more With leaders Bugle A on there bye week the attention switched to the runners up spot with both Mevagissey A and Tregonissey A claiming 4 1 victories to keep things very much up in the air…', null, null, 'Race for 2nd hots up more With leaders Bugle A on there bye week the attention switched to the runners up spot with both Mevagissey A and Tregonissey A claiming 4 1 victories to keep things very much up in the air regarding the chase for silverware The Meva boys dropped the first frame to there D team as Rich Lakeman beat Matt Mills but they responded by taking the remaining games with James Popplewell sneaking home against Ian Latham in the closest of the frames Ryan Bilsons fine 54 break helped Treggy A secure a good win over Bethel A to keep the pressure on Garry Stephens excellent 33 break was enough to put him 53 points up on Barrie Mcintosh who in turn made a 40 clearance to get 4 ranking points but still lost the match but Jason Simmons and Chris Stephenson both won black ball frames to secure the win Len Flower made a 30 break for Pelynt but still lost out to Dave Rundle as Bugle B picked up a couple points in there quest to get away from the bottom of the league Keith Moore got Bugles other frame with Jason Hill John Daniell and Dave Grose getting the home points Treggy B took 3 frames at Bethel D with Paul Baron knocking in a 41 break as he beat Gavin Dyche Stuart Giles and Andrew Gooch took there other frames with Jason Pascoe and Dayle Dyche replying St Neot v Mevagissey B was postponed Mo Roscorla got Bugle Cs only point at home to leaders Bethel C when he defeated Ben Stunell but the victory sees the Bethel boys open up a 5 point lead at the top St Blazey got a good 3 2 win at Bethel B to stand in third place with wins for Richie Bolt Mark Cockayne and Mike Delaney with Wayne Jordan and Clive Stuthridge replying Matt Moore and Darren Biggen put Lostwithiel 2 up at Gorran but were hauled back in by Rob Bunney and Steve Williams and the home side got the win thanks to Mike Wherrys walkover as Losty are still looking for a replacement for John Wilton who has had a shoulder operation Lerryn picked up an excellent 4 1 win at Meva C thanks to wins for John Hancock Terry Middleton Graham Hoskin and Matt Woodward with Darren Powell taking out Charles Mcmiram for the home side', '2020-02-23', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Results and Scores from Week 17 – 2020', 'results-and-scores-from-week-17-2020', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'A great display by Mevagissey D gives there survival chances a massive boost more Mevagissey D put on a great display at home to Bethel D taking all 5 frames to give there survival chances a massive boost Close wins…', null, null, 'A great display by Mevagissey D gives there survival chances a massive boost more Mevagissey D put on a great display at home to Bethel D taking all 5 frames to give there survival chances a massive boost Close wins for Ben Prynn and Rich Lakeman along with victories for Rob Blamey James Tomlinson and Ian Latham means the Meva boys close to within a point of Bugle B with a game in hand The Bugle boys suffered a 4 1 reverse at home to St Neot with Keith Moores win against Chris Perring there only bright spot leaving them with a desperate need of winning frames in there remaining 3 games Leaders Bugle A were involved in a very tight contest at Bethel A as Geoff Hawken and Matt Green took 2 of the first 4 frames with Andrew Best and Ian Ball responding and it looked good for the home side as a break of 35 by Garry Stephens put him 21 points ahead of Gary Spencer but a fantastic clearance of 35 by Spencer won the frame and match Barrie Mcintosh had breaks of 37 and 56 giving Treggy A a good start a Meva B and there were also wins for Jason Cocks and Ryan Bilson giving them the victory with Matt Rowe and Ben Rothwell replying Treggy B got a good win at home to Pelynt as Stuart Giles Damian Rowe and Andrew Gooch won there frames to put them 3 up but the away team got the last 2 frames through Jason Hill and Dave Grose In the Rees League leaders Bethel C had a good night beating Gorran 4 1 Roger Smithsons blackball win over Rob Bunney was cancelled out as Lee Mckinstry beat Leigh Rosevear also on the black but further wins for Ben Stunnel Howard Brett and Courtney Crockford saw the leaders extend there lead at the top St Blazey took 4 frames at home to Meva C to stay in the promotion picture with Adrian Evans stopping the whitewash taking out Mark Cockayne Caz Stephens beat Charles Mcmiram to get Treggy C there solitary point at Lerryn a result which moves the home side up to 5th in the table after victories for Matt Woodward Graham Hoskin John Hancock and Terry Middleton Josh Bristow had the leagues highest break of 46 as he beat Graham Taylor of Treggy D with Jim Tamblyn also winning for Bethel B but Steve Knight Ryan Taylor and Kieron Clemes secured the win to keep the Treggy lads in second place', '2020-03-02', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Results and Scores from Week 18 – 2020', 'results-and-scores-from-week-18-2020', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Bugle A crash to defeat and race hots up for 2nd between Meva A and Treggy A more Mevagissey B had a great week taking 2 frames at St Neot on monday night before taking the scalp of league leaders Bugle B on tuesday…', null, null, 'Bugle A crash to defeat and race hots up for 2nd between Meva A and Treggy A more Mevagissey B had a great week taking 2 frames at St Neot on monday night before taking the scalp of league leaders Bugle B on tuesday Dave Kendall and Mark Gregory got 2 good wins at Neots beating Anthony Maddams and Steve Courts with Darren Lock knocking in breaks of 34 and 35 as he took out Ben Rothwell On Tuesday they went 3 up at Bugle thanks to wins for messers Kendall Rothwell and Chambers with Andrew Best (44 break)and Jake Moore taking the last 2 frames for the champions elect Meva A came from 2 down to beat Bethel A after M Green and Garry Stephens got the away side off to a great start but recovered to win through Mark Ashton Matt Chesterfield and James Popplewell Treggy A are still in the hunt for silverware after they took out relegation threatened Bugle B 4 1 with Dave Rundle stopping the rot by defeating Martin Knight with Barrie Mcintosh having a 43 break to beat Colin Rundle St Neot got 4 frames at home to Treggy B with Geoff Merrimans defeat of Ant Maddams the saving grace Pelynt beat Meva D thursday night by 4 frames to 1 it started well for the visitors as Rob Blamey beat Richard Broad but his team mates all suffered big defeats to leave them still at the bottom league with 3 games to go St Blazey got all 5 frames at Treggy C to stay in promotion contention with Mike Delaney and Chris Wherry both winning on the black Treggy D took 3 points at Meva C to stay second as Keiron Clemes Graham Taylor (36 break) and son Ryan took the first 3 frames with the home side taking the last 2 through Predator Tregale and Darren Elliott Bethel B got all 5 frames at home to Lostwithiel with Jim Tamblyns close defeat of Craig Nicholls the stand out game of the night whilst Bugle C went 3 down at hone to Lerryn but managed to take the final 2 through Nige Couchman and Kevin Spencer', '2020-03-09', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Results and Scores from Week 19 – 2020', 'results-and-scores-from-week-19-2020', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Interesting finish to season as Bugle crash to heavy defeat and new highest break of 88 secured. more A amazing tuesday night saw the leaders of both leagues getting hammered and a new top break in the victory league…', null, null, 'Interesting finish to season as Bugle crash to heavy defeat and new highest break of 88 secured. more A amazing tuesday night saw the leaders of both leagues getting hammered and a new top break in the victory league made by Barrie Mcintosh with a fantastic 88. Pelynt pulled off a fantastic whitewash of tabletoppers Bugle A as Dave Grose beat Gary Spencer in the opener on the black.Easier wins by Len Flower Phil Ormond Richard Broad finished off by John Daniell knocking in a 33 break whilst beating Paul Sturtridge gave them an unbelievable win. That result helped Mevagissey A and Tregonissey A close the gap on the leaders to give us a couple of interesting weeks to finish the season. Meva A picked up a great 4 1 win at St Neot with only Darren Locks victory over Matt Chesterfield saving the whitewash, while Treggy A took 4 points at Bethel D to stay in the hunt as Jason Cocks, Chris Stephenson and Rich Pearson followed Mcintoshs win with Dayle Dyche beating Ryan Bilson to take a precious point for the home side. Meva D got 2 good points against there B team through Ian Latham and James Tomlinson helping them off the bottom of the league going above non playing Bugle B who they play in the last game of the season. Treggy B took out Bethe A with Phil Hooley Stuart Giles and Andrew Gooch victorious with Garry Stephens and Matt Green who knocked in a fine 36 break. St Blazey have blown the Rees League title wide open after beating leaders Bethel C 4 1 and it still means its a 3 way fight in the final 2 weeks for the silverware. 2 black ball frames went the way of the home side with Chris Wherry and Richie Bolt taking them and Stewart Dewings and Mike Delaney got the other frames with Howard Brett taking out Mark Cockayne, in reply Gorran got a good win at Meva C as Lee Mckinstry Steve Williams and the charismatic Rob Bunney pulled through with Darren Powell and the Predator responding Bugle C got 2 good points at Bethel B as Nige Couchman and Phil Johns took out the dangerous Josh Bristow and Wayne Jordan but Jim Tamblyn Guy Buckle and Clive Stuthridge pulled them through. Lerryn continue to do well and beat Lostwithiel 4 1 to stay comfortably in 5 th with Matt Moores defeat of John Hancock saving the whitewash.', '2020-03-13', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('BREAKING NEWS', 'breaking-news', 'League News', '[]'::jsonb, 'BREAKING - St Blazey & District Snooker League postpone amidst CORONA VIRUS concerns. more In light of todays government statement regarding the coronavirus outbreak it has been decided to postpone the season with…', null, null, 'BREAKING - St Blazey & District Snooker League postpone amidst CORONA VIRUS concerns. more In light of todays government statement regarding the coronavirus outbreak it has been decided to postpone the season with immediate effect. This means the final 2 league games the boynton trophy the presentation night and all of the competition finals will not be played. The committee will monitor the situation on an ongoing process with a hope to finish the season at a later date. Concerns had already been raised by players and teams who weren''t willing to play the final fixtures and who can blame them. We hope everyone understands the difficult decision we were forced to make to make tonight and support our decision. The Committee', '2020-03-16', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Cornwall Amateur Billiards and Snooker Association STATEMENT', 'cornwall-amateur-billiards-and-snooker-association-statement', 'League News', '[]'::jsonb, 'With the current health instructions imposed by the government more Together with the guidance from the billiards & snooker governing bodies the WPBSA/ESPB. Decisions on the forthcoming 2020/21 season has been made…', null, null, 'With the current health instructions imposed by the government more Together with the guidance from the billiards & snooker governing bodies the WPBSA/ESPB. Decisions on the forthcoming 2020/21 season has been made by various league committees throughout Cornwall. These decisions have confirmed that various leagues have decided to suspend the new 2020/21 season completely. Another is making a decision at the end of November to establish if a partial season can be run depending on restrictions, and, if they players actually wish to return to play safely. Those leagues with outstanding league matches and/or competitions may try and complete between now and Apr 2021, if the restrictions and guidance allows, and more importantly, if their players or clubs wish to play. Their decision is paramount in the interest of safety. The decisions taken by those leagues, correctly in my mind, impact heavily on the County, and, would make it near impossible to run any competitions during 2020/21, due to either reduced numbers or no participants in any events, not forgetting other leagues yet to decide to suspend operations at a later date. Many clubs have still not opened, some may not at all until this pandemic has gone, and to those clubs that have opened, they have to apply strict instructions and guidance to their members, and supply and enforce PPE equipment is available for the use of club members. The County committee have considered all the above factors and to comply with the government’s instructions and governing bodies recommendations, it has been agreed that in the interest of all players and officials safety, that,the County will be suspending the 2020/21 season with immediate effect. As the County has five remaining finals from the 2019/20 season outstanding, the committee may try and complete them between Jan and Apr 2021, providing the government restrictions and governing bodies guidance permits it, and, more importantly if those players feel safe enough to play. Their decision is paramount and final. I am sure some players throughout Cornwall will be disappointed, but these are difficult and unprecedented times, health is paramount, and our committee act for the benefit of all players, officials and supporters alike. Derek Brooks. Secretary Cornwall Billiards & Snooker Association.', '2020-08-30', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Committee Meeting Update', 'committee-meeting-update', 'League Meetings', '[]'::jsonb, 'After a meeting of the St Blazey and District Snooker League committee held on Monday 24th August more It was decided to try and finish the last 2 league games of the 2019/20 season and all of the competition finals…', null, null, 'After a meeting of the St Blazey and District Snooker League committee held on Monday 24th August more It was decided to try and finish the last 2 league games of the 2019/20 season and all of the competition finals when it is safe to do so depending on government guidelines Obviously we do not expect to see any snooker for quite some time as many of our venues remain closed at present and snooker tables closed The committee will continue to monitor developments and take appropriate actions The 2020/21 season has been cancelled', '2020-09-05', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('We are back and ready to play the 2021-2022 Snooker League', 'we-are-back-and-ready-to-play-the-2021-2022-snooker-league', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Snooker is back from the 28th September more More details to follow and updates on website for fixtures and venues', null, null, 'Snooker is back from the 28th September more More details to follow and updates on website for fixtures and venues', '2021-09-20', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Bugle make strong start', 'bugle-make-strong-start', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2021-2022 Underway - Week 1 - Report more The opening week of the new season saw the first covid cancellation as Bethel A had to postpone there game with St Neot. Bugle A made a very strong start taking all 5…', null, null, 'Season 2021-2022 Underway - Week 1 - Report more The opening week of the new season saw the first covid cancellation as Bethel A had to postpone there game with St Neot. Bugle A made a very strong start taking all 5 points off Mevagissey B with Ian Powell getting a walkover win. Mevagissey D had a great start beating bugle b with wins for Ben Prynn, Matt Chesterfield, James Tomlinson and Ian Latham with Dave Rundle Stopping the whitewash when defeating Rich Lakeman. Len Flower, Phil Ormond, John Daniell and Richard Broad got pelynts 4 frames against Bethel D with Liam Johns defeating the home teams new signing Andrew Gooch. In the Rees league Gorran got all 5 frames against Mevagissey C to sit top of the table early doors as they won 4 frames on the black and Rob Bunney received a walkover. Gladly Lerryn managed to raise a squad to play this season and started With a 3 2 win over Tregonnissey C whose points came from Ryan Orchard and James Beeches. St Blazey a got the better of Bethel B by the odd frames with wins for Billy Vigus, Daley Mcerlain and Mark Cockayne with Craig Nicholls and Adrian Dyche replying and Clive Stuthridge and Jim Tamblyn took 2 points off Bethel C who got the victory through Courtney Crockford Leigh Rosevear and skipper Roger Smithson.', '2021-09-30', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Mevagissey D go joint top after week 2', 'mevagissey-d-go-joint-top-after-week-2', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 2 - Report more Officials Players and Supporters of The St Blazey and District Snooker League came together on tuesday night at 19.30 hrs at there clubs and gave a loud round of applause in…', null, null, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 2 - Report more Officials Players and Supporters of The St Blazey and District Snooker League came together on tuesday night at 19.30 hrs at there clubs and gave a loud round of applause in memory of its President Leighton Varcoe who sadly passed away the previous saturday Loved by all for his charm wit and knowledge of the game he will be greatly missed In the league action itself Meva D are joint top of the Victory League after a finr 3 2 win at St Neot with victories for Rich Lakeman Ian Latham and James Tomlinson with Darren Lock notching a 42 break for the home side Pelynt got a hard earned odd frame victory at Bugle B to also sit joint top through John Daniell Phil Ormond and Len Flowers black ball win over Keith Moore Bethel D got a great win at home to Treggy A by the odd frame Paul Baron got the first for the visitors before Jason Pascoe Liam Johns and Gavin Dyche got the win with Chris Stephenson taking Treggys other point Bethel A got all 5 frames at luckless Meva B who have failed to get a point in the opening 2 games with Mark Gregory and Ben Rothwell both losing out on the black Gorran sit pretty at the summit of the Rees League after a second 5 0 win this time at Treggy C most of the games were tight but went there way including the last frame where a massive 135 points were scored as Mark Wherry beat Lynn Kearns 73 to 62 Kev Spencer and Roy Bayliss got Bugle Cs points against St Blazey A who replied through Daley McErlain and Stewey Dewings and took the win as the home side could only muster 4 players on the night Leigh Rosevear Roger Smithson and Ben Stunell put Bethel C 3 up at Meva C but the home siderallied to take the final 2 frames through Darren Powell and Captain Adrian Evans', '2021-10-07', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Bilson Big Breaks', 'bilson-big-breaks', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 3 - Report more Tregonissey A bounced back from last weeks defeat to take all 5 frames from struggling Bugle B with Ryan Bilson having breaks of 64 and 35 in his win over Dave Rundle.…', null, null, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 3 - Report more Tregonissey A bounced back from last weeks defeat to take all 5 frames from struggling Bugle B with Ryan Bilson having breaks of 64 and 35 in his win over Dave Rundle. Mevagissey D hold the bragging rights over there B team by winning 4 1 to stay top of the table with Ben Rothwell getting his sides first point of the season as he lowered Predator Tregales flag. Bugle A got 4 points at home to Bethel D through Andy Best Paul Sturtridge Ian Powell and Gary Spencer with Jake Moore losing out to Dayle Dyche for the away point. Steve Courts and Darren Lock put St Neot 2 up at Pelynt who bounced back to take the match with wins for Len Flower Phil Ormond and Andrews Gooch. Gorran continue on there merry way as they took out Bethel B 4 1 to stay clear at the top of the Rees league with Darren Biggens defeat of Mark Wheery stopping the whitewash. The St Blazey derby went the way of the B team as the went 3 up through Wayne Jordan Josh Bristow and a Martin Richards walkover with the A team pulling the last 2 frames back as Stewart Dewings knocked in a 42 break and Craig Wheery who did really well to beat. Clive Stuthridge Nathan Taylor got Treggy C off to a great start at Bethel C beating Ben Stunell but that was as good as it got as the home side recovered to take the last 4 frames although how Roger Smithson managed to beat Lynn Kearns was a major talking point on the night and Bugle C got a good 3 2 win at lerryn as Luke Kennedy Roy Bayliss and Kev Spencer who beat the departing Charles McMiram in the decider to seal the win.', '2021-10-14', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Meva D continue great start to the season', 'meva-d-continue-great-start-to-the-season', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 4 - Report more Meva D took 2 points away at Bugle A and went close to causing a really big upset with Ian Latham only losing out on the black to Ian Powell, Matt Chesterfield and Rich Lakeman…', null, null, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 4 - Report more Meva D took 2 points away at Bugle A and went close to causing a really big upset with Ian Latham only losing out on the black to Ian Powell, Matt Chesterfield and Rich Lakeman won their frames to keep them level top of the victory league. Pelynt slipped 2 frames behind to Treggy A as Ryan Bilson and Jason Cocks who knocked in a 30 break as the away side made a good start but John Daniell Richard Broad and Andrew Gooch completed the come back to keep them joint top. Meva B got 4 much needed points at home to Bugle B to climb off the bottom of the table with win for Mark Gregory Pete Chambers Nathan Shaw and Matty Rowe. Bethel A v Bethel D was a covid cancellation. Bugle B were the weeks big winners in the Rees league getting all 5 at Meva C to move up to 4th in the table helped by winning 3 tight frames on the night. Bethel C have joined Gorran at the summit after beating there B team 4 1 with Craig Nicholls taking out Courtney Crockford to avoid the whitewash. Vicki Rollings got Treggy Cs only point as they lost at home to St Blazey B as she beat Sarah Franks and Les Shakespear took out Pete Bate for Lerryn''s solitary point at St Blazey A.', '2021-10-20', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Pelynts first defeat', 'pelynts-first-defeat', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 5 - Report more Meva D inflicted a first defeat for Pelynt as they took top spot in the Victory league with Rich Lakeman taking out John Daniell in the deciding frame to seal the win Meva B…', null, null, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 5 - Report more Meva D inflicted a first defeat for Pelynt as they took top spot in the Victory league with Rich Lakeman taking out John Daniell in the deciding frame to seal the win Meva B are forgetting there early season woes as they got 4 good points away to Bethel D to move up to 5th in the table with Gavin Dyche getting the home team solitary point by beating Mark Gregory Treggy A took the first 3 frames at home to Bethel A with wins for Ryan Bilson Chris Stephenson and Jason Cocks but Bob Stephens and Mark Ashton got the remaining 2 frames for the away side 2 black ball wins helped Bugle C claim all 5 frames at home to Treggy C to move them up to 5th in the table with games in hand on all the teams above them Clive Stuthridge knocked in a 30 break which helped St Blazey B inflict Gorrans first defeat in what is looking a very tight league which paved the way for Bethel C to take top spot in the Rees League as they got 3 frames at Lerryn courtesy of wins for Lee Rosevear Ben Stunell and Roger Smithson Darren Powell and Adrian Evans got Meva Cs 2 points at Bethel B in a game of tight finishes with Josh Doherty Matt Moore and Darren Biggen securing the home win', '2021-11-13', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Team handicap produces some shocks', 'team-handicap-produces-some-shocks', 'Competitions', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2021-2022 - Team Handicap Report more Bethel B picked up a cracking win at Bugle B winning 3 1 as Matt Moore took the winning frame beating Stuart Giles to put his fathers team into the Plate compitition Meva…', null, null, 'Season 2021-2022 - Team Handicap Report more Bethel B picked up a cracking win at Bugle B winning 3 1 as Matt Moore took the winning frame beating Stuart Giles to put his fathers team into the Plate compitition Meva B also produced the goods to sink Bethel A with wins for Dave Kendall Ben Rothwell and captain Mark Gregory Treggy A 3 1 Bugle A Treggy C 1 3 Meva C St Blazey A 0 3 Pelynt St Neot 3 0 Meva D St Blazey B 3 1 Bethel C Bugle C 2 3 Lerryn Bethel D v Gorran postponed', '2021-11-13', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Treggy go break crazy', 'treggy-go-break-crazy', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 6 - Report more Treggy A went break crazy at St Neot as Jason Cocks 43 Paul Barons 33 and Ryan Bilsons 37 helped them whitewash there opponents and move up to second in the Victory league…', null, null, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 6 - Report more Treggy A went break crazy at St Neot as Jason Cocks 43 Paul Barons 33 and Ryan Bilsons 37 helped them whitewash there opponents and move up to second in the Victory league Pelynt lost the first 2 frames at Meva B to Dave Kendall and Ben Rothwell but rallied through Rich Broad Jason Hill and Phil Ormand to win and take top spot Bugle B got 3 points at home to Bethel D to register there first win as Stuart Giles Dave Rundle and Keith Moore won with Dayle and Gavin Dyche replying Gorran got a good 3 2 victory at Bethel C to join there hosts at the top of the Rees League as Lee Mckinstry Rob Bunney and Terry Mills ran out winners with Ben Stunell and Roger Smithson getting the home points Bugle C moved to within a point of the leaders beating Bethel B by the odd frame in a night of 3 black ball finishes Terry Middleton and David Vipond got 2 useful points for Lerryn at St Blazey B who took the win courtesy of Wayne Jordan Clive Stuthridge and Josh Bristow', '2021-11-14', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Bugle A take bragging rights', 'bugle-a-take-bragging-rights', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 7 - Report more Bugle A took the bragging rights as they beat there B team 4 frames to 1 Paul Sturtridges black ball win over Stuart Giles got the ball rolling andwith Gary Spencers 34 break…', null, null, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 7 - Report more Bugle A took the bragging rights as they beat there B team 4 frames to 1 Paul Sturtridges black ball win over Stuart Giles got the ball rolling andwith Gary Spencers 34 break and Andy Best 30 as he whitewashed Keith Moore along with a win for Jake Moore put them 4 up but Dave Rundle took out Ian Powell for the solitary point for the B team Struggling St Neot lost 3 2 at Bethel D to remain winless despite Darren Locks 41 break and Chris Perrings blackball victory over Gavin Dyche with Liam Johns Jason Pascoe and Ross Mcmenemy securing the home win Bethel A picked up a good win at Meva D Rich Lakemans good run carried on as he beat Matt Green but the away side sucured the win through Mark Ashton Bob Stephens Andy Peers and Garry Stephens Gorran stay top of the Rees League by beating Bugle C by the odd frame in a night of 4 very close games Mark Wherry Lee Mckinstry and Terry Mills put the home side 3 up only to be clawed back as Darren Mclaren and Roy Baylisstook the last 2 to take the visitors up to second place Wayne Jordan Josh Bristow and Martin Richards put St Blazey B 3 up away at Bethel B who pulled the remaining frames back through Terry Nicholls and a Darren Biggen walkover Meva C finally registered a win as they came away from Lerryn with a 3 2 win as Predator Tregale and the 2 Darrens of Elliott and Powell got the wins with Terry Middleton and Graham Hoskin replying', '2021-11-18', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Bugles first defeat', 'bugles-first-defeat', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 8 - Report more Tregonissey A have gone joint top of the Victory League after inflicting Bugle A first defeat of the season they were 2 1 down but Martin Knights defeat of Andrew Best and Ryan…', null, null, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 8 - Report more Tregonissey A have gone joint top of the Victory League after inflicting Bugle A first defeat of the season they were 2 1 down but Martin Knights defeat of Andrew Best and Ryan Bilson taking out Gary Spencer sealed the win Meva D continue to amass points and stay joint top after beating Bethel D with wins for Rich Lakeman James Tomlinson and Matt Chesterfield with Liam Johns and Dayle Dyche replying Bethel A took 4 points off Pelynt to move up to joint 3rd as only Phil Ormond could get an away point as Howard Brett Bob Stephens Mark Ashton and Matt Green who knocked in a 36 break took the spoils St Neot finally got off the mark beating Bugle B with Anthony Maddams blackball win over Keith Moore and Darren Locks 40 break the standout points of the evening Gorran stay top of the Rees League after beating Lerryn by the odd frame Lee Mckinstry Rob Bunney and Steve Williams got the home points with John Hancock and Terry Middleton replying Ryan Orchard win over The Predator was Treggy C s only success as Meva D took the remaining 4 frames to move away from the bottom of the table Bethel C went back into second place as the beat St Blazey A by the odd frame with Chris McAvoy inflicting Roger Smithsons first loss of the season', '2021-11-29', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Bethel A go top', 'bethel-a-go-top', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 9 - Report more With Tregonissey A''s game postponed Bethel A go top of the Victory League after taking all 5 frames at Bugle B who slip to the bottom of the table Replacement Howard Brett got…', null, null, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 9 - Report more With Tregonissey A''s game postponed Bethel A go top of the Victory League after taking all 5 frames at Bugle B who slip to the bottom of the table Replacement Howard Brett got the ball rolling beating Colin Rundle further wins for Matt Green Mark Ashton and Bob Stephens who beat the Undertaker left Andy Peers beating Stuart Giles for the nap hand Bugle A have moved up to 2nd after a great 4 1 win at Pelynt with only Richard Broads defeat of Nige Couchman saving the whitewash Meva B had a good 3 2 home win over St Neot Dave Kendall and Mark Gregory and Darren Oshea and Darren Lock had traded frames but in the decider Matt Rowe knocked in a fine 39 break to defeat Ant Maddams to seal the win Rees League leaders Gorran suffered a 4-1 defeat at St Blazey A to damage there title hopes only Lee Mckinstry won for the away side as blazey will by looking to move further up the table when they play there covid cancellation games before xmas Gorrans defeat means they are joined at the top bt Bethel C after they took 4 frames at Bugle C through Courtney Crockford Howard Brett Roger Smithson and Leigh Rosevear with Roy Bayliss beating Pete Smithson for the home point Mark Richards and a Ryan Orchard walkover got Treggy C a couple of points at Bethel B who got the win through Darren Biggen Matt Moore and Terry Nicholls', '2021-12-01', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Bugle A back on top', 'bugle-a-back-on-top', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 11 - Report more There were only 2 games in each league due to covid cancellations but it gave Bugle A the chance to go back to the top of the Victory league which they took by beating…', null, null, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 11 - Report more There were only 2 games in each league due to covid cancellations but it gave Bugle A the chance to go back to the top of the Victory league which they took by beating Mevagissey B by 4 frames to 1 with Nathans Shaws great win by 56 points to 4 over Andrew Best getting the home point Bethel D had a good 4 1 win at home to Pelynt to move right up the table 2 black ball wins for Dayle Dyche and Jason Pascoe made all the difference with Andrew Gooch taking out Ross Mcmenemy in the last game to take the away point Mark Richards and Ryan Orchard put Tregonissey C 2 up at home to Lerryn but the away side responded through Graham Hoskin Lee Shakespear and John Hancock to take the spoils St Blazey A have jumped up to 3rd place in the Rees league with a game in hand on the top 2 after a fine 4 1 win at Bethel B with only Adrian Dyches defeat of Darren Willis', '2022-01-06', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Bethel A top off Victory League', 'bethel-a-top-off-victory-league', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 12 - Report more Bethel A went to the top of the Victory League after beating Meva B 4 frames to 1 Andy Peers reshot black win over Nathan Shaw the closest game on the night with Geoff Hawken…', null, null, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 12 - Report more Bethel A went to the top of the Victory League after beating Meva B 4 frames to 1 Andy Peers reshot black win over Nathan Shaw the closest game on the night with Geoff Hawken going in off the black to give Ben Rothwell a deserved win for the away point Treggy A took all 5 frames at home to Bethel D and with a game in hand on the 2 teams above them look dangerous Ryan Bilson having a 48 break and Rich Pearson a 38 Bugle B are in dire straights after a pointless visit to Pelynt leaving them 8 points adrift at the bottom of the league and heading for the Rees League Meva D picked up a great 4 1 at home to St Neot with wins for Rich Lakeman Rob Blamed Matt Chesto and James Tomlinson with Darren Lock having 2 breaks of 32 and 34 in his win over Ian Latham with Darren O’Shea having a 30 break in his defeat to JT Gorran have gone back to the top of the Rees League after beating Treggy C 4 1 Ryan Orchards win over Steve Williams saved the whitewash as Gorran look in good stead to keep up there promotion bid they move above Bethel C who dropped 2 points at home to a plucky Meva C who deserved more on the night with Charlie Prynn losing out to Ben Stunells last 4 balls great pots to lose the frame St Blazey A are in great shape after getting all the points at home to Bugle C and are only 3 points off the top with a game in hand with Craig Wherry and Chris McAvoy winning 2 close frames on the night', '2022-01-17', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('So tight at the top', 'so-tight-at-the-top', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 13 - Report more Only 3 points separate the top 3 sides at the top of the Victory League after this weeks games. With leaders Bethel A on a bye Bugle A took there chance to regain top spot…', null, null, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 13 - Report more Only 3 points separate the top 3 sides at the top of the Victory League after this weeks games. With leaders Bethel A on a bye Bugle A took there chance to regain top spot taking all 5 frames at Bethel D despite Gav Dyche knocking in a 32 break against Andy Best with the home side also missing out in 2 blackball frames Tregonissey A are only 5 points off the top after getting 4 points at doomed Bugle B as only Dave Rundle defeat of Jason Cocks stopping the whitewash Pelynt rushed into a 3 frame lead at St Neot through Rich Broad. John Daniell and Jason Hill but Darren Locks 41 break and Steve Courts defeat of Len Flower gave a home side a bit of relief It was nip and tuck in the Mevagissey derby as there was never more than 1 frame difference with Nathan Shaws defeat of Rob Blamey in the decider saw the B team have bragging rights over there D team Bethel C took all 5 frames at Treggy C to go back to the top of the Rees League with Ben Stunells black ball win over Ryan Orchard the only close game on the night Bugle C had a great 4. 1 win against Lerryn with only Owen Rounsevell defeat of Kevin Spencer stopping the nap hand St Blazey B beat there A team by the odd frame with win for Martin Richards. Ryan Stephens and Richie Bolt who transferred to the B team earlier in the week with Craig Wherry and Billy Vigus replying', '2022-01-24', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Lerryn into final', 'lerryn-into-final', 'Competitions', '[]'::jsonb, 'Team Handicap - Report more Lerryn marched into the Team handicap final after beating Bethel D despite losing the first frame as Dayle Dyche beat Graham Hoskin but John Hancock took out Ross Mcmenemy to level up then…', null, null, 'Team Handicap - Report more Lerryn marched into the Team handicap final after beating Bethel D despite losing the first frame as Dayle Dyche beat Graham Hoskin but John Hancock took out Ross Mcmenemy to level up then 2 great victories for Les Shakespear and Terry Middleton over Gavin Dyche and Jason Pascoe saw them home In a delayed quarter final Mevagissey B beat St Blazey B 3 0 to set up a semi final against Tregonissey A great wins for Dave Kendall Matty Rowe and Ben Rothwell saw them win a very hard to call game In the Plate competition Bethel A beat Bugle A to move into the final In a marathon first frame lasting 70 minutes Garry Stephens got the home side in front taking out Gary Spencer with Mark Ashton beating Jake Moore in a very close second frame leaving Andy Peers with the help of a fine 41 break to seal the win In the final they will face Mevagissey D who got home 3 1 at St Blazey A in a night of very tight frames James Tomlinson and Rich Lakeman both sneaked home on the pink and black but Stewart Dewings pulled 1 back beating Matt Chesterfield on the black only for Ian Latham to seal the win beating Craig Wherry In 2 rearranged league games Bethel A got a 3 2 win at St Neot on monday evening to move back into 2nd place in the Victory league and faced a massive game at home to 3rd placed Tregonissey A last night Wins for Darren Lock who had a 31 break and Andy Ridgeman put the home side nicely placed but victories for Andy Peers Mark Ashton and Garry Stephens saw Bethel home Bethel C came from 2 down at St Blazey B to win and extend there lead at the top of the Rees League to 6 points Rich Bolt and Josh Bristow gave the the home side a great start but Ben Stunell Leigh Rosevear and Howard Brett got the win for leaders', '2022-02-07', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Treggys big win', 'treggys-big-win', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 14 - Report more Tregonissey A all but ended Bethel A title chances dishing out a 4 1 defeat to Bethel A to move above them into 2nd place with a game in hand on leaders Bugle A Andy Peers…', null, null, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 14 - Report more Tregonissey A all but ended Bethel A title chances dishing out a 4 1 defeat to Bethel A to move above them into 2nd place with a game in hand on leaders Bugle A Andy Peers missed a easy black to gift victory to Ryan Bilson in the opener and Ryan Tonkin potted very well to take out Matt Green in the next followed by Garry Stephens missing a simple blue for frame ball leaving Paul baron to clear up in great style for treggys 3rd frame Jason Cocks then beat a unlucky Mark Ashton on the black with Bethels only point coming as Rich Pearson went in off the black to gift Geoff Hawken the frame Bugle A also got 4 points at home to St Neot with Darren Locks defeat of Gary Spencer the only crumb of comfort for the visitors Andrew Gooch knocked in a fine 50 break on his way to beating Rich Lakeman as Pelynt put there recent poor form behind them taking 4 points off visiting Meva D with Ian Lathams win against Jason Hill getting there point Meva B had a great 5 0 win at home to struggling Bethel D with only Matt Rowes defeat of Jason Pascoe the only close game In a rearranged game on monday night Bugle B picked up a odd frame win over Meva D to move within 6 points of Bethel D who they play next With Rees League leaders on a covid cancellation 2nd placed Gorran closed the gap after a great 3 2 at home to a strong St Blazey B side after being 2 down as Terry Mills Lee Mckinstry and Warren Ball all got wins Treggy C finally got there first win as Ryan Orchard Mark Richards and Nat Rosevear all won there games against Bugle C who replied through Gary Stocks and Justin Oxenham Bethel B got the odd frame win at Meva C as Ady Dyche Craig Nicholls and Darren Biggen all prospered with Darren Powell and Predator Tregale replying for the seasiders', '2022-02-14', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Only 1 point separates top 2', 'only-1-point-separates-top-2', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 15 - Report more Tregonissey A and Bugle A are only 1 point apart at the top of the Victory league going into the last 4 games of the season in the closest finish for years Treggy A got a good…', null, null, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 15 - Report more Tregonissey A and Bugle A are only 1 point apart at the top of the Victory league going into the last 4 games of the season in the closest finish for years Treggy A got a good 4 1 home win against St Neot with Barrie Mcintosh having a 36 break in his first game of the season as he beat Steve Courts and despite having a knock of 31 Ryan Bilson lost out to Darren Lock who had a 36 break Bugle A postponed there game with Bethel A until this week and will be looking for a big win to keep the pressure on Pelynt had another fine win at home to Meva B to sit comfortable in 4th position with wins for Goochy Rich Broad John Daniell and Len Flower with Nathan Shaw taking out Jason Hill to get Mevas point Bugle B are all but down after a 3 2 defeat at Bethel D leaving them with a seemingly impossble task to avoid the drop they got there points with wins for Dave Rundle and Keith Moore but Gavin and Dayle Dyche and Liam Johns sealed the home win St Blazey A have caught up with all there games and now stand 6 points clear at the top of the Rees League having played Mevagissey C twice in a week getting a 4 1 home win and a 3 2 away win with Darren Powell winning both his games for Meva with Darren Elliot getting there other point St Blazey B could still have a big say in things after taking 4 frames at Lerryn who had a Dave Vipond walkover to thank for there point Also Gorran whose game was cancelled are also in the mix as they have 5 games to play in whay is a very interesting end to the season Good wins for Justin Oxenham Kev Spencer and Gary Stocks put Bugle C 3 up away at Bethel B who pulled the last 2 frames back through Ady Dyche and Matt Moore', '2022-02-18', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Big games left - There are some really big games left in both leagues as the last 2 weeks of the season are upon', 'big-games-left-there-are-some-really-big-games-left-in-both-leagues-as-the-last-', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 16 - Report more There are some really big games left in both leagues as the last 2 weeks of the season are upon With teams in both leagues catching up on there postponements there are massive…', null, null, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 16 - Report more There are some really big games left in both leagues as the last 2 weeks of the season are upon With teams in both leagues catching up on there postponements there are massive games being played this week as teams look to seal the league titles In the Rees League St Blazey A got all 5 frames at Tregonissey C to be 6 points ahead of there only challenger Bethel C with the pair playing each other last night Mike Haley knocked in a 36 break at Treggy and there were further wins for Andrew Kitt Billy Vigus Stewart Dewings and Mark Cockayne The Bethel boys got 4 frames at Gorran on wednesday to keep the pressure on with Lee Mckinstry beating Roger Smithson for the home sides only success this followed there 3 2 win at Bugle C the previous evening with wins for Warren Ball Lee Mc and Terry Mills Bethel B got a good 3 2 win at Meva C and picked up a useful 2 points away to St Blazey B with Ady Dyche and Craig Nicholls winning on both nights In the Victory League both Treggy A and Bugle A won on tuesday night 5 0 to be just one point apart with Jason Cocks having breaks of 37 and 38 helping his side get the maximum at Meva B and Andrew Bests 38 and Gary Spencer with a 38 helped there team to whitewash there B team St Neot beat Bethel D 3 2 to move above there opponents in the table and pretty much secured there place in the top division in a night of 3 black ball finishes with Darren Lock knocking in a 45 break as he beat Ross Mcmenemy Bethel A had a good week as after beating Meva A by 4 frames to 1 on the tuesday the upset the title applecart by going to Bugle A on thursday and getting a 3 2 win with Matt Green Garry Stephens and Geoff Hawken doing the damage On friday night Treggy A got all 5 frames at home to Meva D to be 4 points clear of Bugle A going into last nights game between the 2 teams with Bugle needing a big in if they have any chance of winning the title', '2022-02-28', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Almost there', 'almost-there', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 17 - Report more Both Tregonissey A and St Blazey A pulled off great victories over there nearest rivals to need only a single point to seal there league titles going into last nights final…', null, null, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 17 - Report more Both Tregonissey A and St Blazey A pulled off great victories over there nearest rivals to need only a single point to seal there league titles going into last nights final games of the season The Treggy boys beat Bugle A by the odd frame with Barrie Mcintosh beating Andrew Best in the last game to get the win after earlier wins for Rich Pearson and Ryan Bilson with Gary Spencer and Paul Sturtridge getting Bugles frames Subject to any changes at the AGM Bethel D are relegated to the Rees League after finishing there season second bottom but signed off with a 3 2 home win over Mevagissey D Bugle B will also ply there trade in the Rees League and suffered a 3 2 defeat at home to St Neot Mike Williams and Keith Moore got 2 rare wins with Darren Lock Darren Oshea and Steve Courts getting the away points Bethel A secured a minimum of 3rd place with a good win at Pelynt who will finish 4th Garry Stephens knocked in a fine 46 break whilst beating John Daniel and there were further wins for Andy Peers and Matt Green St Blazey B blew away Bethel C and will be champs if the Bethel boys drop any games at home to Lerryn on monday Good victories for Stew Dewings Craig Wherry Billy Vigus and Chris McAvoy got them within touching distance of the trophy with Roger Smithson beating Mark Cockayne for Bethels sole success Treggy C picked up only there second win of the season with a great 4 1 victory at Meva C Ryan Orchard Mark Richards James Raggot and Lynn Kearns all got wins with Darren Powell being the seasiders only winner Gorran are still in the mix for runners up spot after fighting back from 2 down at Lerryn to take the spoils and picked up another 4 points at Bethel B on wednesday and are equal 2nd with St Blazey B who played a double-header at Bugle C losing the 1st game 2 3 but winning the reverse fixture 5 0 to really shake things up going into the final games last night', '2022-03-09', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Champs are crowned - Tregionissey & St Blazey A capture league titles', 'champs-are-crowned-tregionissey-st-blazey-a-capture-league-titles', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 18 - Report more As expected Tregonissey A and St Blazey A secured there league titles in the final league games of the season Treggy only needed 1 point at Mevagissey D but got all 5 with…', null, null, 'Season 2021-2022 - Week 18 - Report more As expected Tregonissey A and St Blazey A secured there league titles in the final league games of the season Treggy only needed 1 point at Mevagissey D but got all 5 with Barrie Mcintosh knocking in a 36 break and Ryan Bilson 42 as they finished the season with 14 wins out of 16 played Bugle A take the runners up spot after beating Pelynt by 4 frames to 1 Andrew Gooch beat Andy Best in the first game to give the visitors a great start but wins for Gary Spencer Ian Powell Paul Sturtridge and stand in Justin Oxenham who knocked in a 32 break closed out Bugles season Bethel A took 3rd place beating relegated Bugle B winning every frame and now look ahead to next weeks team plate final against Mevagissey D St Neot beat Mevagissey B by 4 frames to 1 to move up 2 places in the league with Darren Lock having a 54 break his 10th break over 30 in the season St Blazey A were crowned champs on monday night as Lerryn took a point at Bethel C through David Vipond to leave the blazey boys with a unassailable lead they did lose to Gorran on tuesday by the odd frame with Stew Dewings and Billy Vigus victorious with Rob Bunney Terry Mills and Lee Mcinstry getting the home points as Lee secured the Rees rankings award after many years of trying St Blazey B signed off beating Mevagissey C by the odd frame with wins for Josh Bristow Rich Bolt and Ryan Stephens as the 2 Darrens Elliott and Powell got Mevas points Bethel B finished with a win at Treggy C in a night of 3 very close frames with wins for Darren Biggin Ady Dyche and Craig Nicholls with James Beeches and Dan Tynan replying for the home side', '2022-03-09', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Darren Lock wins the Boynton Trophy for 2022', 'boynton-trophy-2022', 'Competitions', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2021-2022 - Boynton Trophy - Report more 21 players made an early saturday morning start to play in the Boynton Trophy in memory of ex league secretary Gordan Boynton The one frame shootout had plenty of close…', null, null, 'Season 2021-2022 - Boynton Trophy - Report more 21 players made an early saturday morning start to play in the Boynton Trophy in memory of ex league secretary Gordan Boynton The one frame shootout had plenty of close finishes with the handicaps being a great leveller As the matches progressed the semi final matches were Steve Courts against Darren Lock which Darren took on the colours after steve had played excellently all day twice pulling back big handicaps The other semi final saw Josh Bristow defeat a plucky Gavin Dyche to move into the final Josh had a massive 52 start which he increased to 61 points before missing a hard pot and Darren then knocked in a superb 57 break to close the gap and after a few more shots each Darren had a 20 break to put the match out of joshs reach A great day was had by all with several players staying to the end to support the players', '2022-03-25', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Presentation night', 'presentation-night', 'League News', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2021-2022 - Presentation Evening - Report more St Blazey and district Snooker League held there awards evening at Bethel social club on saturday evening with chairman Garry Stephens thanking everyone for there…', null, null, 'Season 2021-2022 - Presentation Evening - Report more St Blazey and district Snooker League held there awards evening at Bethel social club on saturday evening with chairman Garry Stephens thanking everyone for there attendance and led a round of applause in memory of 6 past players who had passed away since the last awards evening List of winners Victory league winners Tregonissey A runners up Bugle A Rees league winners St Blazey A runners up Bethel C Team Handicap winners Tregonissey A runners up Lerryn Plate Handicap winners Mevagissey D runners up Bethel A Boynton Trophy Winner Darren Lock runner up Josh Bristow Victory rankings winner Darren Lock 112 points Rees rankings winner Lee Mckinstry 70 points Victory highest break Ryan Bilson 64 Rees highest break Stuart Dewings 42 Melville Mills Award Jonathon Barron (posthumous award)', '2022-04-05', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Just a reminder that the AGM is tonight (Tuesday 12th July 2022) at Bethel 19:30 start.', 'just-a-reminder-that-the-agm-is-tonight-tuesday-12th-july-2022-at-bethel-1930-st', 'League Meetings', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2022-2023 - Annual General Meeting (AGM) more At LEAST 1 person per club should attend Please bring £30 per team entry money (receipts will be given) If you have not done so by now please let Richard Pearson…', null, null, 'Season 2022-2023 - Annual General Meeting (AGM) more At LEAST 1 person per club should attend Please bring £30 per team entry money (receipts will be given) If you have not done so by now please let Richard Pearson or Clive Stuthridge have all the names of your teams/squad for this coning season, including reserves, and please name the captain and vice captain.', '2022-07-12', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Pelynt make strong start', 'pelynt-make-strong-start', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2022-2023 – Week 1 – Report more After a excellent snooker shoot out competition the previous week won by Josh Bristow the league started with Pelynt taking all 5 frames at home to Mevagissey B to top the…', null, null, 'Season 2022-2023 – Week 1 – Report more After a excellent snooker shoot out competition the previous week won by Josh Bristow the league started with Pelynt taking all 5 frames at home to Mevagissey B to top the first league table of the season with wins for John Daniell Len Flower Rich Broad Andrew Gooch and Nigel Doble. Bugle A came away from Mevagissey A with 4 points with Ben Prynn beating Ian Powell for the home side with Rob Blamey losing on the black ball to Justin Oxenham. Gary Spencer knocked in a 35 break whilst beating Charlie Prynn. In the battle of the 2 promoted teams St Blazey A pipped Bethel C by the odd frame with wins for Chris McAvoy liam Reynolds and Mark Cockayne. In the Rees league St Blazey B claimed a very good win at Bethel D with victories for Josh Bristow new signing Gavin Dyche and Clive Stuthridge with Tyrone Stephens and Geoff Hawken replying. Bugle C made an excellent start to the campaign beating Bethel B by 4 frames to 1 with Craig Nicholls stopping the whitewash In a incredible frame Gary Stocks beat Ady Dyche by 82 points to 80. Lerryn got off to a flyer at home to Tregonissey B winning 4 1 Owen Simpson beating Terry Middleton for the away side with Graham Hoskin and John Hancock both winning on the black. Predator Tregale and Darren Elliott secured 2 points for Mevagissey C at Gorran Haven with home wins for Lee McKinstry Rob Bunney on the black and Terry Mills also on the black.', '2022-09-29', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Tregonissey A make strong start to season', 'tregonissey-a-make-strong-start-to-season', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2022-2023 – Week 2 – Report more Victory league defending champions Tregonissey A made a solid start to there campaign beating Bethel C 4-1 with wins for Paul Baron Ryan Bilson Geoff Merriman and Jason Cocks…', null, null, 'Season 2022-2023 – Week 2 – Report more Victory league defending champions Tregonissey A made a solid start to there campaign beating Bethel C 4-1 with wins for Paul Baron Ryan Bilson Geoff Merriman and Jason Cocks with Howard Brett beating Rich Pearson for the home point. Andrew Gooch knocked in a 33 break helping Pelynt come away from St Neot with the add frame victory Nigel Doble and Richard Broad were also winners with Steve Courts and Darren Lock replying. Bethel A started there season winning 4 1 at Mevagissey B with Dave Kendall taking out Bob Stephens for the home point with Mark Ashton Garry Stephens Matt Green and Andy Peers victorious for the visitors. St Blazey A picked up 2 useful points at Bugle A through Chris McAvoy and Mark Cockaynes black ball win against Justin Oxenham with Andrew Best Gary Spencer and Ian Powell getting the home points. Bugle C good start continued winning 3 2 at Mevagissey C Dave McLaren and Roy Bayliss both won black ball frames with Gary Stocks also winning with the 2 Darrens of Powell and Elliott winning for the seasiders. Bugle B started life in the Rees with a great 4 1 win at Tregonissey B with wins for Keith Moore Stuart Giles, Dave and Colin Rundle who put together a fine 38 break, Owen Simpson beat Mike Williams for the hosts. Lee McKinstry and Terry Mills got Gorran Havens points at St Blazey B who had Gavin Dyche Ryan Stephens and Josh Bristow to thank for there victory. And Bethel B got there first win beating Lerryn by the odd frame Craig Nicholls Matt Moore and Darren Biggen won there frames with James Stephens and Graham Hoskin replying.', '2022-10-07', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Pelynt continue great start to season', 'pelynt-continue-great-start-to-season', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2022-2023 – Week 3 – Report more Pelynt''s good start to the season continued as they took 4 frames at home to Bethel C as only Courtney Crockfords defeat of John Daniell saved the whitewash with the home side…', null, null, 'Season 2022-2023 – Week 3 – Report more Pelynt''s good start to the season continued as they took 4 frames at home to Bethel C as only Courtney Crockfords defeat of John Daniell saved the whitewash with the home side taking the last 2 frames on the black ball Tregonissey A got a good 3 2 home win over Bugle A with win for Jason Cocks Ryan Bilson and Martin Knight with Andrew Best and Gary Spencer replying In the Mevagissey derby the B team took bragging rights by defeating the A team by the odd frame Wins for Mark Gregory Matt Mills and Nathan Shaw saw them home with Rich Lakeman who knocked in a 34 break and Rob Blameys black ball win over Matt Rowe getting the A teams frames Bethel A romped into a 3 frame lead at home to St Neot with Bob Stephens Garry Stephens and Matt Green victorious but the visitors secured the final 2 frames through Steve Courts and Darren Lock St Blazey B jumped to the top of the Rees League after getting 4 frames at Bugle C Roy Bayliss beat Clive Stuthridge to take the home sides single point with Josh Bristow Gavin Dyche Richie Bolt and Martin Richards the winners for the table toppers Bugle B are looking to bounce back straight away to the Victory League and took all 5 frames at home to Bethel B with Keith Moore beating his son Matt in the 4th frame of the evening there were other wins for Mike Williams Stuart Giles and Dave and Colin Rundle The 2 Darrens of Mevagissey C put them 2 up at Lerryn by beating Terry Middleton and John Hancock respectively but the hone side bounced back to take the spoils through Graham Hoskin David Vipond and Les Shakespeare Owen Simpson and Ryan Orchard got Treggy C off to a great start at Bethel D beating Steve Benallack and Jason Pascoe but the home side took the final frames through Dave Morshead Tyrone Stephens and Ross McMenemy', '2022-10-14', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Bugle A go top', 'bugle-a-go-top', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2022-2023 – Week 4 – Report more With Pelynts game postponed Bugle A moved to the top of the Victory league with a 4 1 win at Mevagissey B. It started well for the home team as Nathan Shaw hammered Justin…', null, null, 'Season 2022-2023 – Week 4 – Report more With Pelynts game postponed Bugle A moved to the top of the Victory league with a 4 1 win at Mevagissey B. It started well for the home team as Nathan Shaw hammered Justin Oxenham but that was there only success as Jake Moore Gary Spencer (breaks of 33 and 30) Paul Sturtridge and Andrew Best secured a big win for away side Bethel A took all 5 frames against there C team to move joint 2nd and face a tough match next as they go to Tregonissey A who took 4 frames at St Blazey A through Geoff Merriman Rich Pearson Jason Cocks and Ryan Bilson with Stuart Dewings taking out Chris Brown for the home point St Blazey B got 4 frames at Tregonissey B to stay top of the Rees league with Owen Simpsons defeat of Clive Stuthridge the only brightspot for the home side Bugle B move into 2nd place after whipping Gorran Haven 4 1 as Stuart Giles Dave and Colin Rundle and Keith Moore all won with Steve beating Mike in the battle of the Williams to secure the visitors point Bethel D suffered a 3 2 defeat to there B team to continue there inconsistent start to the season Tyrone Stephens and Steve Benallack got there points with Dave Morshead going in off after potting the black to gift Craig Nicholls the win with Ady Dyche and Matt Moore completing the win Lerryn picked up a good win at Bugle C in a night of close frames with victories for Les Shakespeare Terry Middleton and David Viponds blackball win over Kevin Spencer with Nige Couchman and Keiran Pearce replyong', '2022-10-21', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Latest Competition Results', 'latest-comp-results', 'Competitions', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2022-2023 – Competition Results – Report more Singles g spencer 3. 2 p baron R Bilson 2. 3 d lock Doubles k Moore/s Giles 0 3 g spencer/a best Doubles handicap Craig/terry Nicholls 0 3 Bob Stephens/Andy peers…', null, null, 'Season 2022-2023 – Competition Results – Report more Singles g spencer 3. 2 p baron R Bilson 2. 3 d lock Doubles k Moore/s Giles 0 3 g spencer/a best Doubles handicap Craig/terry Nicholls 0 3 Bob Stephens/Andy peers R orchard/m Haworth 3 2 d Biggen / m Moore Seniors prelims J Daniell 1. 3 r smithson P baron 0 3 d Vipond Bill toms A peers. 3. 2 c Stuthridge B Stephens. 3. 1 g spencer D Tregale. 0. 3. C Rundle O Simpson. 2. 3. G Stephens G dyche. 3. 0. G Merriman R orchard. 3. 2. K Moore S Giles. 1. 3. L Reynolds Willie Thomas M Moore. 3. 0. C Nicholls', '2022-11-05', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Tregs go top', 'tregs-go-top', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2022-2023 – Week 5 – Report more Tregonissey A went to the top of the Victory league by beating St Neot in a rearranged league match Ryan Bilson took out Darren Lock on the black to get the ball rolling and…', null, null, 'Season 2022-2023 – Week 5 – Report more Tregonissey A went to the top of the Victory league by beating St Neot in a rearranged league match Ryan Bilson took out Darren Lock on the black to get the ball rolling and there were further wins for Martin Knight Geoff Merriman and Jason Cocks who had a 37 break against Darren Oshea with Steve Courts getting the visitors point by beating Rich Pearson Team Handicap results Preliminary Round St Neot 3 0 lerryn First Round St Blazey B 0 3 Tregonissey A Bugle C 0 3 Mevagissey A Bethel C 2 3 Tregonissey B Bugle B 2 3 Pelynt', '2022-11-05', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Bugle A go break crazy', 'bugle-a-go-break-crazy', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2022-2023 – Week 6 – Report more Bugle A went break crazy at home to Bethel A and lead the table by 5 points albeit having played more games than Bethel A who lie 2nd and Tregonissey A in 3rd place Andrew Best…', null, null, 'Season 2022-2023 – Week 6 – Report more Bugle A went break crazy at home to Bethel A and lead the table by 5 points albeit having played more games than Bethel A who lie 2nd and Tregonissey A in 3rd place Andrew Best 33 Jake Moore 38 and Paul Sturtridge with a 39 got there breaks with Gary Spencer and Justin Oxenham also winning Bethel A got 4 good points at home to Pelynt with Paul Woodmans black ball defeat of Tyrone Stephens the only success for the visitors Mevagissey B are on a hot streak and move up to 4th after beating St Blazey A 5 0 with wins for Dave Kendall Nathan Shaw Ben Rothwell Matt Rowe and a walkover for Mark Gregory whose opponent failed to show up Mevagissey A went 2 up at St Neots through Rob Blamey and Rich Lakeman but a walkover for Ant Maddams and wins for Steve Courts (36 break)and Darren Lock(31 break) saw the home side hit back for the win St Blazey B march on at the top of the Rees League after taking all 5 frames at home to Lerryn with Clive Stuthridge knocking in the highest break so far in the league with a 46 Bethel D got a really good 4 1 win at home to Bugle B to move into 3rd place in what looks like a very interesting race for the title Wins for Steve Benallack Jason Pascoe Tyrone Stephens and Liam Jones got the victory with Dave Rundle successful for the visitors Tregonissey B picked up there first win beating Gorran Haven by the odd frame Amanda Fleming Owen Simpson and Ryan Orchard won there frames with Terry Mills and Warren Ball replying Bethel B came home from Mevagissey C with 4 frames to pull themselves off the bottom of the league to be replaced by there opponent', '2022-11-14', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Victory league leaders suffer surprise defeat', 'surprise-defeat', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2022-2023 – Week 7 – Report more Victory league leaders suffered a surprise defeat at Pelynt losing by the odd frame Andrew Gooch and John Daniell had put the hosts 2 up but Gary Spencer and Andrew Best…', null, null, 'Season 2022-2023 – Week 7 – Report more Victory league leaders suffered a surprise defeat at Pelynt losing by the odd frame Andrew Gooch and John Daniell had put the hosts 2 up but Gary Spencer and Andrew Best levelled things up only for Nigel Doble to beat Jake Moore to secure the home win. Second place Bethel A took all 5 frames at Mevagissey A to close the gap on the leaders with Matt Green knocking in a 30 break and Mark Ashton having a 39. Tregonissey A also took all 5 frames at home to Mevagissey B winning 2 blackball frames and Ryan Bilson knocking in a 52 break in the final frame of the evening. St Neot took the first 3 frames at St Blazey A through Darren Lock Steve Courts and Andrew Tamblyn with the home side taking the last 2 with wins for Liam Reynolds and Mark Cockayne. St Blazey B storm on at the top of the Rees league getting the maximum frames at Bethel B with home captain Craig Nicholls unlucky to lose the last frame to Richie Bolt by potting the white ballwhen on the final black. Bugle B lost the first frame at home to Mevagissey C as Adrian Evans took out Mike Williams but wins for Keith Moore who had a 44 break Dave and Colin Rundle and Stuart Giles sees them sit 2nd in the table. Bethel D suffered a odd frame defeat at Gorran Haven who had Lee McKinstry Terry Mills and Warren Ball to thank for there win with Jason Pascoe and Steve Benallack who had a 34 break winning for the visitors with Tyrone Stephens also knocking in a 34 in his defeat to Warren. Tregonissey B got a great win at Bugle C to move up to 5th in the table with the unbeaten Owen Simpson Paul Simpson and Ryan Orchard getting wins with Roy Bayliss and Gary Stocks replying.', '2022-11-17', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Bethel A go top of the league', 'bethel-a-go-top-of-the-league', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2022-2023 – Week 8 – Report more Bethel A went to the top of the Victory League after taking all 5 frames at home to St Blazey Garry and Bob Stephens put them 2 up with Mark Ashton beating Liam Reynolds in a…', null, null, 'Season 2022-2023 – Week 8 – Report more Bethel A went to the top of the Victory League after taking all 5 frames at home to St Blazey Garry and Bob Stephens put them 2 up with Mark Ashton beating Liam Reynolds in a tight 3rd frame and with Matt Green and Andy Peers also winning it sets up a big game between Bethel and Bugle A next week Mevagissey A picked up 4 good points at home to Bethel C leaving there opponents well adrift at the bottom with only Howard Bretts defeat of Rob Blamey there only success St Neot beat Meva B 4 1 with Steve Courts and Chris Perring both winning blackball games and Darren Lock having a 32 break whilst beating Mark Gregory with Nathan Shaw beating Andrew Tamblyn for the away point Bugle B remain in 2nd place in the Rees League after beating Lerryn 4 1 with Terry Middleton beating Colin Rundle in the final frame for the visitors point Gorran Havens good season continued with a 4 1 win at home to Bethel B as Terry Mills Steve Williams Warren Ball and Lee McKinstry all won with Craig Nicholls beating Rob Bunney for the away teams point Bethel D stay 3rd after getting 4 points at home to Bugle C Jason Pascoe Geoff Hawken Liam Jones and a Ross McMemeny walkover got there points with Gary Stocks taking out Steve Benallack on the black for the visitors frame', '2022-11-25', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('2 big wins for Treggy A', '2-big-wins-for-treggy-a', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2022-2023 – Week 9 – Report more Tregonissey A got 2 big wins this week to move up to 2nd place in the Victory league On tuesday they took 4 points off Mevagissey A with only Rob Blameys defeat of Geoff…', null, null, 'Season 2022-2023 – Week 9 – Report more Tregonissey A got 2 big wins this week to move up to 2nd place in the Victory league On tuesday they took 4 points off Mevagissey A with only Rob Blameys defeat of Geoff Merriman stopping the full house And then in a re-arranged game they beat leaders Bethel A again taking 4 frames Rich Pearson beat Andy Peers in the opener then Ryan Bilson knocked in a 35 break to inflict Garry Stephens first defeat of the season There were further wins for Jason Cocks and Paul Baron with Mark Ashton taking out Geoff Merriman for Bethels point with the gap at the top now only 2 points with Treggy having played a game less Bethel had a fine victory at Bugle A by the odd frame with Gary Spencer having a 37 defeat when beating Matt Green St Neot got 4 frames at Bethel C to move up to 4th place with Darren Lock knocking in a 30 break when beating Ben Stunell the home frame saw Martin Powell beat Chris Perring St Blazey A suffered a 3 2 loss at home to Pelynt for who Nigel Doble Andrew Gooch and Richard Broad won with Andrew Kitt and a Chris McAvoy walkover replying In the Rees league Bethel D took all 5 frames at Mevagissey C as they try to chase down the top 2 with Liam Jones blackball win over Darren Elliot the only real tight frame of the night Gorran Haven got a great full house at Lerryn with Steve Williams single point win over Les Shakespeare helping them to the maximum points Matt Moore, Terry Nicholls and Craig Nicholls who took Owen Simpsons unbeaten record were Bethel Bs winners as they defeated Tregonissey B who replied through Ryan Orchard and Amanda Fleming In the Bugle derby the B team beat the C team by 4 frames to 1 to close the gap on leaders St Blazey B who were without a game Keiran Pearce beat Mike Williams to got the C teams only point with another 2 frames very close on the night', '2022-12-12', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Team handicap week', 'team-handicap-week', 'Competitions', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2022-2023 – Team Handicap – Update more It was team handicap week in the St Blazey and district snooker league and there were a lot of very tight frames over the 2 competitions Pelynt picked up a great 3 1 win…', null, null, 'Season 2022-2023 – Team Handicap – Update more It was team handicap week in the St Blazey and district snooker league and there were a lot of very tight frames over the 2 competitions Pelynt picked up a great 3 1 win at Bethel A with Andrew Gooch very impressive beating Bob Stephens in the opener and then Richard Broad knocked in a very 44 break when taking out Andy Peers Matt Green pulled one back for the home side against Nigel Doble but Len Flower beat Garry Stephens in the next to seal the victory Tregonissey A went through against St Blazey A as Jason Cocks Paul Baron and Geoff Merriman all won with Pete Bate replying Joining them in the semi final draw will be there B side as they got the better of Mevagissey A They went into a 2 0 lead with wins for Amanda Fleming and Owen Simpson only for Rob Blamey to beat Ryan Orchard in the next but Mark Richards beat Ben Prynn in the 4th frame to seal the win St Neot against Mevagissey B was postponed In the Plate competition Bugle B won a very tight game against St Blazey B to progress Stuart Giles won on the black against Josh Bristow in the 1st game then Dave Rundle had a big win over Richie Bolt Clive Stuthridge got the better of Mike Williams to pull one back only for Colin Rundle to beat Martin Richards again on the black to seal the win Mevagissey C took the 1st 2 frames at home to Bethel C who then conceded the game as they only arrived with 4 players and couldnt win so Meva went through Bugle C dug deep to defeat Bethel B in a game switched to there venue as 3 Bethel sides had been drawn at home Ady Dyche and Terry Nicholls had put Bethel 2 1 up sandwiched by Nige Couchmans win against Matt Moore only for Keiran Pearce and Garry Stocks to take the final 2 frames fot the win Steve Benallack drew first blood for Bethel D at home to Bugle A beating Paul Sturtridge with Garry Moore defeating Ross McMenemy to level up In the 3rd frame Jason Pascoe raced into a 35 point lead against Jake Moore who managed to pull the deficit back and take the lead only for Jason to take green to pink to seal the win In the next frame Geoff Hawken managed to keep his points advantage against Andrew Best helped by a very scrappy table to seal the win for the home side', '2022-12-15', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('New leaders in the Victory league', 'new-leaders-in-the-victory-league', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2022-2023 – Week 10 – Report more With Bethel A on there bye week Tregonissey A went to the top of the Victory league as a result of there 3. 2 win at St Neot. They got off to a flyer with Jason Cocks knocking…', null, null, 'Season 2022-2023 – Week 10 – Report more With Bethel A on there bye week Tregonissey A went to the top of the Victory league as a result of there 3. 2 win at St Neot. They got off to a flyer with Jason Cocks knocking in a 43 break in the opener against Chris Perring and further wins for Rich Pearson and Geoff Merriman put them 3 up But the home side fought back through Steve Courts and Darren Lock who inflicted a first defeat of the season on Ryan Bilson Bugle A took 4 frames at home to Mevagissey A to stay in 3rd place Rich Lake man beat Justin Oxenham in the opener for meva’s point but the home side responded through Andrew Best. Gary Spencer. Ian Powell and Dave Rundle Mevagissey B got a great win at home to Pelynt with victories for Matt Rowe Nathan Shaw and Matt Mills who had a 30 break whilst defeating Len Flower In the Rees league leaders St Blazey B crashed to a 4 1 defeat at home to Bethel D which really tightens things up at the top as only Josh Bristows defeat of Geoff Hawken there only bright spot as wins for Tyrone Stephen. Steve Benallack Jason Pascoe and Liam Jones all won there games for the away side In the only other game played in the league Bugle C came away from Berhel B with a 3. 2 win Kieran Pearce. Roy Bayliss and Kev Spencer all won with Darren Biggen and Craig Nicholls replying for the home side', '2023-01-04', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Big wins for top 3', 'big-wins', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2022-2023 – Week 11 – Report more All 3 teams at the top of the Victory league got big wins to maintain a very tight race for the title Leigh Rosevear got bottom side Bethel C off to a great start at leaders…', null, null, 'Season 2022-2023 – Week 11 – Report more All 3 teams at the top of the Victory league got big wins to maintain a very tight race for the title Leigh Rosevear got bottom side Bethel C off to a great start at leaders Tregonissey A by beating Geoff Merriman but Rich Pearsons responded to level the match before Jason Cocks with.the aid of a 35 break and 2 breaks of 34 and 43 by Ryan Bilson together with Paul Barons black ball win over Ben Stunell got the points for the front runners. Bethel A also dropped the first frame at home to Mevagissey B as Dave Kendall took out Bob Stephens but with Mark Ashton Garry Stephens (35 break)Matty Green and Andy Peers all winning it makes sure they keep the pressure on at the top Bugle A got all 5 points at St Blazey A to move into joint 2nd with Ian Powell just getting the better of Liam Reynolds in the 3rd frame and Gary Spencer winning a close 4th beating Mark Cockayne Richard Broads 47 break and Andrew Goochs fine 56 got Pelynts frames at home to St Neot with Darren Oshea and Steve Courts both winning close games along with Darrens Locks victory sealing the away win Pelynt also played on table 2 to catch up a postponed game and beat Mevagissey A taking all 5 frames Robert Gasgogne s close win against Ben Prynn got them on the way followed with wins for Nigel Doble Rich Broad Len Flower and Andrew Gooch completed a very good evening for him as he knocked in a 39 break to go with his 56 earlier on in the night Bugle B cut the gap at the top of the Rees League to St Blazey B to 4 points with a game in hand as they took all the frames at home to Tregonissey B with big victories for Mike Williams Keith Moore Dave Rundle and Stuart Giles with Colin Rundle just getting the better of Mark Haworth Leaders St Blazey B dropped a game at Gorran Haven with Lee McKinstry beating Gavin Dyche and had Clive Stuthridges black ball win over Rob Bunney in the last to thank for getting 4 points as Josh Bristow Martin Richards and Richie Bolt also won there games Lerryn and Bethel B as usual battled out a odd frame match with the home side prevailing through James Stephens John Hancock and David Vipond with Terry Nicholls and Matt Moore replying Nigel Couchman put Bugle C ahead at home to Mevagissey C only for Adrian Evans to level things up Gary Stocks restored the lead but once again the away side fought back through Darren Elliott only for Keiran Pearce to have a walkover in the last to seal the win', '2023-01-11', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Big win for Bethel', 'big-win-for-bethel', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Season 2022-2023 – Week 12 – Report more With the Bugle A and Tregonissey A game postponed Bethel A got a great 4 points at St Neot to top the Victory league by 3 clear points Steve Courts beat Matt Green in the…', null, null, 'Season 2022-2023 – Week 12 – Report more With the Bugle A and Tregonissey A game postponed Bethel A got a great 4 points at St Neot to top the Victory league by 3 clear points Steve Courts beat Matt Green in the opener to get the home side off to a good start but Garry Stephens beat Darren Lock to level thinks up and the away side moved ahead thanks to Mark Ashtons 42 break when beating Ant Maddam and with further wins for Andy Peers and Bob Stephens the table toppers returned home happy In the Mevagissey derby the B team handed out a 5 0 thrashing to they A team who are really in a relegation dogfight Matt Rowes blackball victory against Darren Powell being the only tight game on the night Leigh Rosevears nerve gangling respotted black ball win against Paul Woodman got bottom side Bethel C off to a good start at home to Pelynt but the away team took the next 3 frames through Len Flower Andrew Gooch and Nigle Doble with Howard Brett defeating Richard Broad for the home sides second point All of the top sides in the Rees League dropped points but Bugle B have now closed the gap on leaders St Blazey B to 3 points with a game in hand after beating Bethel B 4 1 who got there only frame as Adrian Dyche played excellently to defeat Dave Rundle Nige Couchman and Kieran Pearce both won as Bugle C came away from St Blazey B with 2 frames with Josh Bristow Clive Stuthridge and Gavin Dyche winning for the home side Bethel D dropped 3 points at Treggy B which really damages there title chances Steve Benallack and Geoff Hawken got them off to a great start putting them 2 up but wins for Mark Haworth Mark Richards and Owen Simpson got the home win Meva C got there 1st win of the season beating Lerryn 4 1 as Adrian Evans Darren Elliott Dave Tregale and Mark Ferguson all won with Les Shakespear having a walkover for the away point', '2023-01-23', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Season 2022-2023 – Week 13 – Report', 'season-2022-2023-week-13-report', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Tregonissey narrow gap at top of Victory League more With both Bethel A and Bugle A dropping a couple of frames in there matches Tregonissey A closed in on the top of the Victory league after beating St Blazey A 4 1…', null, null, 'Tregonissey narrow gap at top of Victory League more With both Bethel A and Bugle A dropping a couple of frames in there matches Tregonissey A closed in on the top of the Victory league after beating St Blazey A 4 1 with Liam Reynolds having a 31 break in the last frame of the night against Martin Knight to claim a much needed point for the Blazey boys as they fight to get away from the bottom end of the table. Bethel A lost the 1st frame against there C team as Ben Stunell took out Bob Stephens but wins for Matt Green Mark Ashton and Andy Peers put them back in control but a great win for Roger Smith son over Garry Stephens secured another valuable point. Mevagissey B picked up 2 good points at Bugle A as Matt Mills beat Andrew Best and Ben Rothwell hammered Jake Moore with Justin Oxenham Gary Spencer and Paul Sturtridge getting the home frames. Darren Powell and James Tom Linton put Mevagissey A 2 up at home to Pelynt who recovered to get the win through Paul Woodman Len Flower and Nigel Dobles Blackwall win over Ben Prynn. St Blazey B took 4 points at home to Tregonissey B with Clive Stuthridge knocking in a 44 break and Josh Bristow a 30 with Ryan Orchard beating Martin Richards for the away point. Lee McKinstry was Gorrans only winner at home to Bugle B who keep up the pressure on the Blazey boys as Colin and Dave Rundle Mike Williams and Keith Moore registered wins. Bethel D are hanging on to the top 2s shirt tails as they got 4 points against there B team as Craig Nicholls beat Steve Benallack to stop the whitewash. Bugle C came home from Lerryn with 3 points with wins for Gary Stocks birthday boy Kev Spencer and Keiran Pearce with John Hancock and a Graham Hoskin walkover getting the points.', '2023-01-29', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('League, Competitions & draw Update', 'league-competitions-draw-update', 'Competitions', '[]'::jsonb, 'League, Competitions & draw Update more Mevagissey B reached the Team Plate handicap final after a great win at home to Tregonissey A by 3 frames to 1 Geoff Merriman got Treggy off to a great start beating Dave…', null, null, 'League, Competitions & draw Update more Mevagissey B reached the Team Plate handicap final after a great win at home to Tregonissey A by 3 frames to 1 Geoff Merriman got Treggy off to a great start beating Dave Kendall but with Ben Rothwell getting the better of Richard Pearson and Matt Mills Black ball defeat of Jason Cocks it was left to Nathan Shaw using full advantage of his handicap start to beat Ryan Bilson and send his side into the final where they will play Pelynt who beat Tregonissey B 3 1 Len Flower took the first frame against Lynne Kearns to get Pelynt rolling but Treggy levelled up when Mark Richards beat Richard Broad but with Nigel Doble and Andrew Gooch both winning they progressed to the final In the Plate competition Bugle B came from 2 down against there C team to win Gary Stocks and Dave McLarens close win over Mike Williams had the underdogs tasting glory but Keith Moores 31 break and big wins for Stuart Giles and Colin Rundle got the B team home They will play Bethel D who came home from Mevagissey C with a 3 0 win Jason Pascoe potted well to beat Adrian Evans in the opener and with Steve Benallack edging pass Louise Winterburn next up Ross McMenemy Big win over Mark Ferguson to seal the deal In a rearranged Victory league game Bethel C picked up there 1st win of the season beating fellow strugglers St Blazey A by the odd frame to give themselves hope of avoiding the drop Courtney Crockford Roger Smithson and Leigh Rosevear were there winners with Liam Reynolds and Mark Cockayne getting Blazeys frames Singles Semi-Final Best of Five Frames Home player to contact opponent by Friday 10th February 2023. To be played by Saturday 25th February 2023. Garry Stephens (Bethel) v Andrew Best (Bugle) Darren Lock (St Neot) v Gary Spencer (Bugle) Bill Toms Semi-Final Best of Five Frames Away player received 5 points extra to handicap Home player to contact opponent by Friday 10th February 2023. To be played by Saturday 25th February 2023. Andrew Best (SCR) (Bugle) v Winner of (Ryan Bilson (SCR) v Jason Cocks (+7)) Garry Stephens (+7) (Bethel) v Chris Perring (+35) (St Neot) Seniors Semi-Final Best of Five Frames Away player received 5 points extra to handicap Home player to contact opponent by Friday 10th February 2023. To be played by Saturday 25th February 2023. Geoff Hawken (+21) (Bethel) v Andy Peers (+12) (Bethel) Keith Moore (+30) (Bugle) v Bob Stephens (+21) (Bethel) Willie Thomas Semi-Final Best of Five Frames Away player received 5 points extra to handicap Home player to contact opponent by Friday 10th February 2023. To be played by Saturday 25th February 2023. Owen Simpson (+45) (Tregonissey) v Ryan Orchard (+40) (Tregonissey) Clive Sturthridge (+25) (St Blazey) v Richard Bolt (+30) (St Blazey)', '2023-02-03', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Season 2022-2023 – Week 14 – Report', 'season-2022-2023-week-14-report', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'First defeat of the season for Tregonissey opens up 3 points lead for Bethel more Bethel A inflicted Tregonissey A s first defeat of the season to open up a 3 point lead at the top of the Victory league but have…', null, null, 'First defeat of the season for Tregonissey opens up 3 points lead for Bethel more Bethel A inflicted Tregonissey A s first defeat of the season to open up a 3 point lead at the top of the Victory league but have played a game more than there opponents Bob Stephens beat Geoff Merriman in the opener with Jason Cocks knocked in a 32 break to restore parity by just squeezing past Andy Peers and Ryan Bilson close win over Mark Ashton put treggy ahead only for Matt Green and Garry Stephens big win over Paul Baron and Rich Pearson secured the win St Neot got a good win at home to Bugle A by the odd frame with wins for Ant Maddams Darren Lock and Darren Oshea with Gary Spencer and Andy Best who knocked in breaks of 31 and 39 getting the away points St Blazey A picked up a very importent victory at home to Mevagissey A to help there cause of avoiding relegation in a night of very close frames Billy Vigus and Andrew Kitt put them 2 up with Matt Chesterfield pulling 1 back beating Pete Bate but Liam Reynolds beat James Tomlinson to get the win with Ben Prynn getting Mevas 2nd point when taking out Mark Cockayne In the battle of the top 2 in the Rees League leaders St Blazey B beat Bugle B by the odd frame to open up a 4 point lead at the top but have played a game more than there opponents Liam Johns first game of the season ended in a win along with wins for Clive Stuthridge and Richie Bolt who beat Dave Rundle with Stuart Giles and Keith Moore posting the home wins Bethel D got all 5 frames at home to Lerryn to stay with an outside chance of promotion Ross McMememys close win over Terry Middleton in the opener was followed by big wins for Liam Jones Steve Benallack Geoff Hawken and Jason Pascoe Tregonissey B also picked up all 5 frames at home to Mevagissey C with wins for Mark Richards Mark Haworth Owen Simpson Amanda Fleming and Ryan Orchard Gorran returned home from Bugle C with 3 points with a good win as Terry Mills Steve Williams and Lee McKinstry all won with Roy Bayliss and Kieran Pearce successfull for the home side', '2023-02-10', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Season 2022-2023 – Week 15 – Report', 'season-2022-2023-week-15-report', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Bugle A get 2 big wins more Bugle A have jumped right into the Victory league title race after 2 really big wins. At the end of last week they inflicted a 4 1 defeat to understrength Tregonissey A with Gary Spencer…', null, null, 'Bugle A get 2 big wins more Bugle A have jumped right into the Victory league title race after 2 really big wins. At the end of last week they inflicted a 4 1 defeat to understrength Tregonissey A with Gary Spencer having a 34 break beating Paul Baron and Andrew Best knocking in a 32 against Jason Cocks there were further wins for Jake Moore and Paul Sturtridge with Rich Pearson getting past Justin Oxenham for Treggys point. Then on tuesday night they got all 5 frames at Bethel C to sit just 1 point behind leaders Bethel A having played a game more Dave Rundles blackball win over Ben Stunell got them off to a good start and they finished the evening with Andrew Best having a 30 break as he beat Howard Brett. Bethel A took all 5 frames at Pelynt for a great win which is normally a place they struggle to win with all the games won by a comfortable margin. Mevagissey A got a great home win over St Neot winning 4 frames to give themselves a great chance of avoiding relegation Ben Prynns blackball victory over Chris Perring got the ball rolling and although Darren Lock levelled things up big wins for Matt Chesterfield Darren Powell and James Tomlinson sealed the deal. St Blazey A have hit a wall and are struggling to get frames under there belt and went down again at home to Mevagissey B by 4 frames to 1 with only Stuart Dewings winning against Dave Kendall. Leaders of the Rees league St Blazey B lost the first frame at Lerryn as Terry Middleton beat Martin Richards but recovered to take the remaining games although John Hancock pushed Richie Bolt all the way and likewise James Stephens against Gavin Dyche. Bethel D got a massive 4 1 win at Bugle B to move above them into second place Dave Rundles hammering of Liam Jones in the final frame saved the whitewash after Geoff Hawken Tyrone Stephens Steve Benallack and Jason Pascoe took ahe away points. Mark Haworth put Treggy B ahead at Gorran Haven only for Lee McKinstry and Rob Bunney tp put the home side ahead but Amanda Flemings blackball win over Terry Mills and a win for Owen Sinpsonagainst Steve Williams saw the points go back to Treggy.', '2023-02-17', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Season 2022-2023 – Week 16 – Report', 'season-2022-2023-week-16', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Bethel A nearly there more Bethel A took 4 frames at home to Mevagissey A on monday night to stay top of the Victory League leading Bugle A by 1 frame with a game in hand Rich Lakeman beat Bob Stephens to give Meva a…', null, null, 'Bethel A nearly there more Bethel A took 4 frames at home to Mevagissey A on monday night to stay top of the Victory League leading Bugle A by 1 frame with a game in hand Rich Lakeman beat Bob Stephens to give Meva a great start in there fight to stay up but wins for Andy Peers Mark Ashton(33 break) Garry Stephens and Matt Green saw the leaders home Bugle A got a good 4 1 home win over Pelynt with Keith Moore Ian Powell Andrew Best (31 break) all winning with Paul Woodman taking out Justin Oxenham for the away point Bethel C produced a great 4 1 win at Mevagissey B on monday night to enhance there chances of staying up het went 4 up through Howard Brett Roger Smithson Ben Stunell and Leigh Rosevear with Nathan Shaw beating Courtney Crockford for the home point The Following night the Meva boys took the last 2 frames of the evening against Tregonissey A to dent there opponents chance of silver ware Owen Simpson Barrie McIntosh and Rich Pearson put Treggy 3 up but 2 blackball victories for Mark Gregory and Ben Rothwell pulled frames back for the home side St Blazey B have all but clinched the Rees League title as they took 4 frames at home to Bethel B and are 5 points clear of Bethel D having played a game more Josh Bristows 30 break and Gavin Dyches 36 along with wins for Rich Bolt and Martin Richards saw them 4 up but Craig Nicholls took out Clive Stuthridge in the last frame of the night foe Bethels point Bethel D took all 5 frames at home to Gorran to remain ahead of Bugle B by a single point with both teams having 2 games left Comfortable wins for Steve Benallack Geoff Hawken Tyrone Stephens and Liam Jones put them 4 up with Jason Pascoe beating Lee McKinstry in a close final frame for the nap hand Bugle B kept up the pressure on the top 2 by taking all 5 frames at Meva c and will be ready to pounce if there are any slip ups Big wins for Dave Rundle Keith Moore Colin Rundle (walkover) Mike Williams and Stuart Giles got there frames in what is a very interesting run in Bugle C got 3 frames at Tregonissey B with wins for Nige Couchman Kieran Pierce and Garry Stocks with Owen Simpson and Mark Haworth replying', '2023-02-24', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('League, Competitions & draw Update', 'league-competitions-draw-update-2', 'Competitions', '[]'::jsonb, 'League, Competitions & draw Update more Singles Andrew Best v Darren Lock Mevagissey social club Monday 13th march 19.30 hrs Referee T B C Team Handicap Pelynt v Mevagissey B St Blazey football club Tuesday 14th…', null, null, 'League, Competitions & draw Update more Singles Andrew Best v Darren Lock Mevagissey social club Monday 13th march 19.30 hrs Referee T B C Team Handicap Pelynt v Mevagissey B St Blazey football club Tuesday 14th march 19.30 hrs Referee Mark Cockayne Team Plate Handicap Bugle B V Bethel D Mevagissey social club Wednesday 8th March 19.30hrs Referees K Moore/G Hawken', '2023-02-27', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Confirmed Finals', 'confirmed-finals', 'Competitions', '[]'::jsonb, 'League, Competitions & draw Update more Team Plate Handicap final Wednesday 8th march Mevagissey Social Club Bugle B V Bethel D Referee Dave Kendall Willie Thomas Final Wednesday 8 th March Bethel social club Clive…', null, null, 'League, Competitions & draw Update more Team Plate Handicap final Wednesday 8th march Mevagissey Social Club Bugle B V Bethel D Referee Dave Kendall Willie Thomas Final Wednesday 8 th March Bethel social club Clive Stuthridge +25 V Ryan Orchard +40 Referee Darren Biggen Singles Final Monday 13th March Mevagissey Social Club Darren Lock V Andrew Best Referee Rob Blamey Team Handicap Final Tuesday 14th march St Blazey Football Club Pelynt V Mevagissey B Referee Mark Cockayne Bill Toms Final Thursday 16th march St Blazey football club Andrew Best Scr V Garry Stephens +7 Referee T B C Doubles Handicap Final Monday 20th March Bethel Social Club Matt Green/Mark Ashton +10 V Andrew Peers/Bob Stephens +17', '2023-03-03', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Season 2022-2023 – Week 17 – Report', 'season-2022-2023-week-17-report', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Bethel A and St Blazey B clinch titles more Bethel A clinced the Victory League title as they got the 5 frames they needed at St Blazey A and cant be caught landing the league title for the first time in the clubs…', null, null, 'Bethel A and St Blazey B clinch titles more Bethel A clinced the Victory League title as they got the 5 frames they needed at St Blazey A and cant be caught landing the league title for the first time in the clubs history Matt Green beat Andrew Kitt in the final frame of the evening to win the title after earlier wins for Bob Stephens Andy Peers Garry Stephens and Mark Ashton Tregonissey A and Pelynt played a double header to catch up a postponed game and the home side notched a win by the single frame in both matches Paul Baron knocked in a 46 break and Jason Cocks had a 31 but was beaten by Andrew Gooch with Treggy one point off second place Bugle A going in to the final game of the season last night Darren Lock had breaks of 32 and 42 helping St Neot leave Mevagissey B with the odd frame win Darren Oshea and Anthony Maddams also won with Matt Mills and Dave Kendall getting the home points Mevagissey A all but secured there top league status beating doomed Bethel C by the odd frame as Ben Prynn Rich Lakeman and Darren Powell all won with Leigh Rosevear and Roger Smithson replying St Blazey B clinched the Rees League title after getting 4 frames at Mevagissey C and both Bethel D and Bugle B droping points Josh Bristows 35 break helped him stay top of the rankings and there were wins for Liam Johns Clive Stuthridge and Martin Richards with Adrian Evans getting Mevas point beating Gavin Dyche Les Shakespeare took the final frame of the evening beating Stuart Giles to stop Bugle B from moving into second place as Bethel D dropped 2 frames at Bugle C and they went into last nights final games locked together on 53 points Bugle C frames were won by Roy Bayliss and Kieran Pearce with Geoff Hawken Liam Jones and Ross McMenemy getting Bethels points Bethel B lost by the odd frame on consecutive nights to Mevagissey C then Gorran Haven but managed to move up a place in the league Adrian Evans Mark Ferguson and Louise Winterburn got Meva a welcome win with Rob Bunney Terry Mills and Steve Williams getting Gorrans points', '2023-03-03', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Season 2022-2023 – Week 18 – Report', 'season-2022-2023-week-18-report', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Darren Lock hits superb 120 clearance, and final positions in the leagues confirmed more A superb total clearance of 120 by Darren Lock of St Neot was the big talking point on the last night of the league season…', null, null, 'Darren Lock hits superb 120 clearance, and final positions in the leagues confirmed more A superb total clearance of 120 by Darren Lock of St Neot was the big talking point on the last night of the league season although there are still some issues to be sorted. St Neot went on to win there game against already relegated by them maximum 5 0 ended the season in 6th place Bugle A got a good 3 2 win at champions Bethel A to seal the runners up spot and also taking home the runabout shield after inflicting the home sides second defeat of the season. Ian Ball made a very welcome return to snooker and beat Garry Stephens in the opener and played like he had never been away further wins for Gary Spencer who remained unbeaten all season and Andrew Best saw them home Tregonissey A needed to beat Bugle As result to have a chance of runners up spot but could only match the 3 points as they won at Mevagissey D with James Tomlinsons 31 break in the final match of the night against Jason Cocks handing Bugle A the silverware St Blazey A got 2 points at Pelynt but that was not good enough to save them from relegation Richard Broad Andrew Gooch (37 break) and Nigel Doble had put the home side 3 up with Liam Reynolds and Billy Vigus pulling the final 2 frames back There has to be a playoff between Bethel D and Bugle B to see who gets promoted as runners up in the Rees league as the both only managed to take 3 points in there respective games Bethel had Steve Benallack Tyrone Stephens and Liam Jones(35 break) to thank for there points as Adrian Evans and Darren Elliott took Mevagissey Cs frames and a blackball win by Roy Bayliss over Keith Moore after Kieran Pearce had earlier beaten Colin Rundle meant Bugle B came up just short Gorran Haven rounded off there year by beating Lerryn 4 1 and sealed 4th place in the table and Tregonissey B suffered defeat at home to Bethel B by the odd frame as Adrian Dyche Terry Nicholls and Matt Moore won for the visitors with Ryan Orchard and Owen Simpson replying', '2023-03-10', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Annual General Meeting 2023 (AGM)', 'annual-general-meeting-2023-agm', 'League Meetings', '[]'::jsonb, 'The 2023-2024 snooker season starts on September 26th', 'St Blazey and District snooker league A G M held at Bethel social club on Tuesday 25th July 2023', null, 'Present: K Moore (vice chairman) G Hawken (secretary) R Pearson, C Stuthridge, D Biggen, G Spencer (all committee) C Nicholls, T Nicholls, C Perring, A Evans, R Blamey, M Gregory, A Best J Daniell, I Ball, M Green, R Smithson, R Orchard, J Hancock, T Middleton S Courts Apologies: >G Stephens (chairman) L McKinstry (Gorran haven)

Vice chairman opened meeting at 19.30hrs and thanked everyone for their attendance. The secretary read the minutes of last year''s meeting and these were signed as a true record

1. Secretary had delayed purchasing a new trophy but will replace the Victory League winners trophy for next season
2. British masters tickets were not purchased due to rising costs so Spot the cue ball will never be done again
3. Victory league winners Bethel A v ROTL was played at Tregonissey with the ROTL winning 3 1
4. Rees league winners St Blazey B v ROTL was played at Bethel with the ROTL winning 3 0
5. Online banking was now set up making it easier for players/clubs to pay competition entries etc
6. Rees runabout shield would start at Lerryn next season as last seasons winners Bethel D had been promoted

The league had new sponsors; Build Cornwall who would pay £500 for the next 3 years. Also, K P Accountants and Cornwall Stairs would pay £250 a year again for 3 years to have there logos on either sleeve. New sports shirts with the league badge and the 3 sponsors logos could be purchased from Lex Dezigns in St Austell for £26 each and the secretary would liase with clubs who wished to purchase the shirts.

To add a bit of fun to the Boynton trophy players would be asked to pay a small amount and they would then be backing a fellow player. The winner would receive 50% runner-up 30% and the losing semi-finalists 10% each Committee would speak to players throughout the season to establish the most popular entry fee.

Secretary explained that he would distribute fixture sheets and new league rule sheets to all clubs as soon as possible scorecards were handed out to club representatives at the meeting.

He finally thanked everyone for their help over the season especially the committee members for all of their input and all there help on presentation night.

1. An excellent presentation night raffle and Bethel club paying 100% of the bands cost helped the league keep a healthy balance of £1607.05<
2. League and competition entries amounted to £820 with the trophies and engraving costing £836.64 so a small loss occurred and the snooker shootout clocks and batteries cost £17.29 but overall, a decent year
3. Mark Cockayne and Liam Reynolds are running 2 shootout tournaments before the start of the new season at St Blazey and had posted details on social media
4. The new season would start on Tuesday 26th September with the final league games on Tuesday 12th March 2024
5. Boynton trophy was set for Saturday 16th March 2024
6. Secretary was checking with Bethel club about presentation night to pick a date with suitable entertainment

Secretary asked teams to try and support the team pairs competition as only 5 teams entered last season. A discussion then took place with lots of people giving reasons for not entering teams, such as;

1. Hard to get 6 players
2. Lateness of the games
3. Travelling home too late

So after a lengthy debate it was decided to retire the 6 a side competition and trophy and introduce a new 4 a side comp. The away side would alter the order of the players after the 1st two frames had been drawn so nobody played each other twice. 4 frames would be played until the end and points recorded as before – this was agreed by all present.

John Daniell then spoke about how Jonathan Barron always used to do the “Sealed Handicap Awards” to present at presentation night. John showed a photo of the trophy but was unaware of who won it last and could possibly be in a club which was now closed or no longer in the league. The secretary would get all the details from John and bring to the next AGM for discussion as to reintroducing the competition.

President Chris Perring raised the fact that the Liskeard leagues website always updated competition results as they were given to the secretary, so it was agreed that all results must be posted to the leagues email so Clive Stuthridge, the competition secretary, could update asap. Clive has also done a lot of work on the leagues previous history which he would be posting on the website.

There being no other business, the vice chairman thanked everyone for their input on the evening and closed the meeting at 20:50hrs.

1. Committee proposed Mr Chris Perring to be our new president – carried unanimously. Chris thanked everyone for their support.
2. Committee to alter rule 12 to: “Any rearranged games must be played within 28 days. The team cancelling will be given 3 dates by opponents to play and must play with a minimum of 3 players or concede the game and be fined £20”. After a full discussion, this was carried unanimously.
3. Lerryn: If a team has 4 players, 1 player is drawn twice for a valid game – maximum of 3 times a season. A player can only play 1 extra game per season and no ranking points will be given for that extra game. After a full discussion this was carried unanimously.', '2023-07-25', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('The 2023-2024 snooker season fixtures, teams, players and handicaps are now available', 'new-season-is-upon-us', 'League News', '[]'::jsonb, 'Fixtures & Handicaps for the new season 2023/2024 are now available', 'For this new season we wanted to do something a bit different and make a better effort to keep all our players and members upto date on a more regular basis.', 'Making competition and league results available is our top priority this season', 'This applies not just to Tuesday league matches but to all the competiton results as they happen and when we get the results in will will be putting them on the website as soon as possible

Below you will find links to the Victory League and Rees Memorial League Fixtures and a link to the newly updated Handicaps for all registered playing members for the 2023/2024 season', '2023-09-01', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Gooch wins Snooker Shoot Out', 'andrew-gooch-wins-2023-snooker-shoot-out', 'Competitions', '[]'::jsonb, 'Latest Fixtures & Results from the Snooker Shoot Out Competition 2023-2024', 'To kickstart the 2023/24 Season, St Blazey FC held their second Shootout Tournament, now becoming the annual curtain raiser of the season.', null, 'A full field of 20 people entered this year having 4 Preliminary Rounds, one of which seen reigning champion Josh Bristow take an early exit to Tregonisseys Ryan Orchard.

We also had the county doubles pairing of Mark Ashton and Matt Green drawing each other, with Matt Green coming out on top in a close frame 46-41.

Going into the last sixteen there was no less than 8 St Blazey representative''s hoping to keep the crown in house for the second year running.

Clive Stuthridge with the win of the round sealing a 47-42 win over Bethels Matt Green, topping it off with a fantastic 30 break.

The other noticeable win going to Andrew Gooch against Chairman Garry Stephens by 60-16, knocking in a 33 Break on the process.

The Quarter Finals seen two all St Blazey ties, Gavin Dyche beating Chris Brown 31-17 and Andrew Kitt pipping Liam Reynolds 39-32. Another good victory for Clive beating Bethel''s Kieran Pearce 58-14 and Andrew Gooch continued his break building with a 51 break to seal a 20 point victory against Justin Oxenham, 77-57.

Now in the money rounds, Gavin Dyche and Andrew Kitt both took £10 home semi finalists losing respectively to Clive and Gooch.

Gooch carried on his potting streak in the Final knocking in yet another 38 break to over come Clive 75-18 taking £50 home in the process with an additional £10 for the highest break. Clive takes £20 as runner up.

1. P1 - Harrison Burdon 50 (18) v Dayle Dyche 40 (13)
2. P2 - Keith Moore 37 (15) v Liam Reynolds 46 (11)
3. P3 - Josh Bristow 41 (8) v Ryan Orchard 49 (18)
