  ('Committee Meeting 05-09-2023', 'committee-meeting-05-09-2023', 'League Meetings', '[]'::jsonb, 'Latest Committee Meeting News', 'St Blazey and District snooker league - Committee meeting held on Tuesday 5th September at Bethel social club with a 19.30hrs start', null, 'Present: C Perring (president)G Stephens (chairman)G Hawken (Secretary)D Biggen Gary Spencer C Stuthridge M Green Mark Cockayne Rich Pearson (all committee) Apologies: K Moore (vice chairman)

Chairman opened meeting and welcomed Chris Perring and Matt Green to there first meeting. Prior to the start of the meeting the preliminary and first round draw of the team handicap draw took place. The minutes of the last meeting were read and agreed as a true record

1. Secretary reported that he had still not heard anything from the Godolphin League but he would resend a text and email to them
2. The Liskeard league are very keen to play an end of season interleague match which will be set up at a later date
3. Chris Perring had been voted as President at the AGM
4. Sponsorship, Rich Pearson had managed to get 2 new sponsorship deals with KP Accountants and Cornwall Stairs both for £250 a year for 3 years. There Logos would go on the sleeve of the new league shirts
5. The cost of the shirts had risen to £24 each but the league would charge £26 each to cover the £20 charge for setting up the machinery to do each clubs logo Bethel and St Blazey had ordered and paid for there''s and the secretary was now getting the trial shirts out to other teams that were interested to get there orders
6. The Team Pairs was discussed at the AGM and after a long discussion it was agreed to retire the 6 a side competition and trophy and run a new 4 a side one with a new trophy The new competition would have the away team alter the order of there players after the first 2 frames so that nobody will play each other twice which was carried unanimously
7. Committee meeting minutes had been sent out to captains after the last meeting and will continue to do so
8. The Boynton trophy players would pay money to play from this season they would then be drawn out a players name if that player gets into the final or semi final they would receive prize money Winner 50% Runner-up 30% Losing semi finalists 10 % This was carried unanimously at the AGM committee members will speak to players during the season to gauge amount they want to pay
9. Lerryn proposal at the AGM was passed unanimously - If a team has only 4 players 1 player is drawn twice for a valid game Maximum of 3 times a season A player can only play 1 extra game per season and no ranking points will be given for that extra game
10. Secretary reported that all 3 sponsorship amounts had been paid into league account
11. Tregonissey C had entered a new team to bring Rees league back up to 9 teams
12. A long discussion was then held re our website. President Chris Perring stated that the Liskeard league website was updated straight away after results had been submitted and asked why our results are hard to find also draws etc, Rich Pearson said that players need to be more proactive by posting results/news on Facebook and agreed with Chris who said the most important people are the leagues players so we need to update ASAP with what''s happening
13. Rich had done a lot of work designing fixture list/handicap sheets where he had removed a lot of players names who no longer play anymore as this was causing issues/new rules sheet/new shirt order forms/ and had done a lot of work to make sure the website is a lot better this year and in ongoing years
14. All results from competitions will now need to be texted to Clive Stuthridge so he can update the Web His name and number will be put on the draws for results to be sent to him
15. Rich Pearson would also have a training session with Clive, Garry, Mark before the season starts and explain everything they need to know as they all now have access to the site
16. There being no further business the chairman closed the meeting at 20.55 hrs', '2023-09-13', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('2023 snooker season underway', '2023-snooker-season-underway', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Match Report - Week 1 - 2023-2024', 'The seasons opening games of the St Blazey and District snooker league gave a wide range of results.', 'Joint early leaders in the Rees league are Gorran and Tregonissey B who both got maximums', 'In the Victory league Mevagissey B got a great result at Pelynt with wins for Matt Mills, Matt Rowe and Dave Kendall with Andrew Gooch and Len Flower replying.

Bugle A got 3 points at Mevagissey A to get there season underway as Gary Spencer, Andrew Best and Paul Sturtridge all won with Ben Prynn and Matt Chesterfield getting the home points.

The battle of the 2 promoted sides St Blazey B and Bethel D went the way of the away team looking resplendent in there new league shirts.

After Liam Reynolds put the home side ahead beating Tyrone Stephens the away team took the next 3 through Ross McMenemy, Jason Pascoe and Geoff Hawken who had a 22 clearance to pip Josh Bristow with Clive Stuthridge beating Steve Benallack in the final frame.

Joint early leaders in the Rees league are Gorran and Tregonissey B who both got maximums Terry Mills Warren Ball Lee McKinstry Rob Bunney and Steve Williams all won there frames against a new looking Mevagissey C.

Also a new looking Treggy C got possession of the runabout shield as the got all the frames at Lerryn with wins for Mark Haworth, Nathan Taylor, Darren Roberts, Kyle Bennetts, and Ryan Orchard.

Bethel B took 4 frames at Tregonissey C who also fielded 3 new players with Newby Lee Hobbs getting the solitary home point taking out Terry Nicholls in the night opener.

The 2 relegated sides met at Bethel as the C team entertained St Blazey A and it was the away team who prevailed with wins for Liam Reynolds, Andrew Kitt and Chris Brown with league sponsor James Smithson and Howard Brett who beat Mark Cockayne on the black getting the home frames

Team Results

Team Standings

Related News', '2023-09-26', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Bugle''s nap hand as they jump to the top of the Victory league', 'bugles-nap-hand', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Match Report - Week 2 - 2023-2024', 'Bugle A took all 5 frames at home to St Blazey B to jump to the top of the Victory league.', 'St Blazey A went 2 up at home to Gorran haven through Andrew Kitt and Mark Cockayne', 'Jake Moore Black ball win over Dale Dyche was followed by a big win for Justin Oxenham and Keiran Pearce along with Andrew Best won there frames on the Black despite Josh Bristow having a 37 break against Andrew with Gary Spencer knocking in breaks of 45 and 29 against Mark Cockayne to complete the nap hand

Tregonissey A started there campaign with the odd frame win at Bethel D with wins for Jason Cocks newcomer Kevin Harris and Richard Pearson with Steve Benallack and Liam Jones replying

Darren lock got St Neot off to a flyer at home to Pelynt knocking in a 32 break as he beat Nigel Doble John Daniell levelled things up beating Chris Perring but wins for Ant Maddams Steve Courts and Darren Oshea who sunk the black to pip Len Flower saw the home side off to a good start

Defending champs Bethel A were pushed all the way at Mevagissey B as Nathan Shaw and Ben Rothwell won there frames for the home side with Mark Ashton and Matt Green along with Bob Stephens replying in a very late night due to a power cut

Stuart Giles Nige Couchman and Keith Moore put Bugle B 3 up at Tregonissey B only to be pulled back as Darren Roberts and Kyle Bennetts won for the home side but Bugle got there hands on the Runabout shield

St Blazey A went 2 up at home to Gorran haven through Andrew Kitt and Mark Cockayne but the visitors responded with Terry Mills and Lee McKinstry victorious but the home side got the win as Chris Brown knocked in 35 break when whitewashing Rob Bunney

Craig Nicholls won Bethel Bs first frame and Matt Moore the last at home to Lerryn who took the win through John Hancock Les Shakespeare and Graham Hoskin

Mevagissey C got 4 frames at home to Tregonissey C with Mark Ferguson Richard Tamblyn who won twice using the new league rule and Adrian Evans all successful with Lee Hobbs getting the away point

