  ('A week of breaks sees Pelynt win first game of the season', 'a-week-of-breaks-sees-pelynt-win-first-game-of-the-season', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Match Report - Week 3 - 2023-2024', 'Andrew Gooch made breaks of 47 and 37.', 'Tregonissey B stay top of the Rees league as Kyle Bennetts, Ryan Orchard.', 'Helping Pelynt get there first win of the season as they beat Bethel D by the odd frame Richard Broad and Len Flower also won with Tyrone Stephens and Ross McMenemys Black ball win over Nigel Doble getting the away points

In the Mevagissey Derby the B team took 4 frames off there A team and sit in 2nd place in the league Darren Powells defeat of Dave Kendall was the A teams only success as Mark Gregory Matt Rowe Nathan Shaw and Ben Rothwell all won very tight games

Bugle A got a good win at Tregonissey A to stay top with Andrew Best and Justin Oxenham and Gary Spencers big final frame win over Phil Hooley securing the Victory with Jason Cocks and Geoff Merriman replying

Darren Lock and Steve Courts put St Neot 2 up at Defending champs Bethel A who fought back to win through Mark Ashton Andy Peers and Matt Greens close winner over Darren Oshea

St Blazey A got 4 points at Tregonissey C to move up to 2nd Darren Elliott put the home side ahead as he beat Billy Vigus but big victories for Liam Reynolds Mark Cockayne Andrew Kitt and Chris Brown took the win

