  ('Tregonissey A surge up the Victory League table', 'tregonissey-a-surge-up-the-table', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Match Report - Week 4 - 2023-2024', 'Tregonissey A have jumped up to 2nd place in the Victory league after 2 victories this week', 'Jason Cocks fired in a fine break of 52 to top the breaks chart', 'On Monday night in a rearranged game they beat St Neot by the odd frame as they took the first 3 frames through Kevin Harris (31 break)Rich Pearson and Geoff Merriman with Steve Courts and Darren Lock pulling back the last 2 frames for the visitors.

Then on Tuesday they got 4 points at St Blazey B with Jason Cocks knocking in a fine 52 break when beating Gavin Dyche with further wins for Kevin Harris Harrison Burdon Geoff Merriman with Josh Bristow getting the home points.

Bugle A stay top after beating Mevagissey B Keiran Pearce put them ahead only for Mark Gregory to level up and Nathan Shaw took the scalp of Andrew Best to put the home side ahead but Justin Oxenhams black ball defeat of Dave Kendall followed by a big win for Gary Spencer got the leaders home.

Mark Ashton and Matt Green secured narrow wins against there D team to put them 2 up only for Geoff Hawken to pull a game back by beating Bob Stephens but with Garry Stephens having a 47 break and Andy Peers a 31 they secured 4 points.

Ben Prynn beat John Daniell to stop the whitewash as Pelynt beat Mevagissey A with Richard Broad (47) and Andrew Gooch (31)getting big wins with Len Flower and Nigel Doble also victorious.

Bethel C took all 5 frames against there B team for there 1st win with Courtney Crockford and Howard Brett both winning tight games with wins as well for James and Roger Smithson and Leigh Rosevear.

Tregonissey C Also got there 1st win going 3 up on Lerryn as Amanda Fleming, Lee Hobbs and Jamie Hobbs all won with David Vipond and Les Shakespeare pulling back the final 2 frames.

Bugle B remain unbeaten after beating Gorran Haven by the odd frame with Keith Moore''s Black ball win over Warren Ball sealing the win Nige Couchman and Dave Rundle also won for the home side with Rob Bunney and Lee McKinstry getting the away points.

