  ('Presentation night 22-23', 'presentation-night-22-23', 'League News', '[]'::jsonb, null, null, null, null, '2023-10-18', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Team Handicap last 16 results', 'team-handicap-last-16-results', 'Competitions', '[]'::jsonb, 'Match Report - Week 1 - 2023-2024', 'The team handicap matches failed to get any shock results although several games were very close', 'Roger Smithson and Leigh Rosevear put Bethel C 2 up against there D team', 'St Neot beat Tregonissey B on Monday night and played Bugle B on Tuesday and Colin Rundle got the visitors off to a good start taking out Steve Courts but Ant Maddams levelled things up beating Mike Williams then Darren lock had breaks of 57 and 32 as he beat Nigel Couchman and the home side progressed to the quarter finals after Nigel Collins beat Keith Moore

Harrison Burden and Phil Hooley put Tregonissey A 2 up at home to Mevagissey A Darren Powell pulled a frame back when defeating Rich Pearson but then Kevin Harris beat Matt Chesterfield for Treggy to progress

Bob Stephens and Matt Green (31 break) put Bethel A 2 ahead against Tregonissey C who levelled up as Lee Hobbs and Amanda Fleming beat Garry Stephens and Mark Ashton respectively leaving Andy Peers to defeat Kelly McMullen in the decider for Bethel to sneak home

Roger Smithson and Leigh Rosevear put Bethel C 2 up against there D team who fought back to win through Liam Jones Steve Benallack and Jason Pascoe

Ian Powell (34) and Andrew Best (47) along with Gary Spencer helped Bugle A beat Pelynt 3 to 1 with Nigel Doble beating Justin Oxenham for the away side

John Hancock put Lerryn ahead at home to Mevagissey B as he took the prized scalp of Nathan Shaw but that was the home sides only success as Matt Rowe Mark Gregory and Dave Kendall got big wins to take the Meva boys through

In the St Blazey Derby there was never more than a frames difference all night. Gavin Dyche and Ryan Stephens took the 1st and 3rd frames for the B side with Liam Reynolds and Chris Brown getting the 2nd and 4th frames for the A team leaving Martin Richards to beat Andrew Kitt in the final game to get the B team home

And finally Bethel B overcame Mevagissey C on Thursday night taking the first 3 frames Darren Biggen beat Richard Tamblin in the opener and the next 2 games were decided on the Black ball as Terry Nicholls edged past Adrian Evans and Glyn Tamblin going in off the black after potting it to gift Ady Dyche the game

