  ('Rees league looking to be a very tight championship race', 'week-6-2023-headline-goes-here', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Match Report - Week 6 - 2023-2024', 'Bugle A have moved 4 points clear at the top of the Victory league after a great win at home against St Neot.Justin Oxenham knocked in a fine 38 break in the opener whilst beating Ant Maddams then Gary Spencer gave Darren Lock his 1st defeat of the season with wins for Andrew Best and Ian Powell putting them 4 up with Steve Courts pulling a frame back beating Keiran Pearce', 'Mevagissey B can count themselves unlucky to lose 4-1 at Bethel D losing 2 frames on the Black ball', 'Mevagissey A picked up there 1st win with a 3-2 victory at home to St Blazey B Wins for James Tomlinson Ben Prynn and Darren Powell secured the points with Josh Bristow and Gavin Dyche replying

Bethel A remain unbeaten after beating Tregonissey A by the odd frame Rich Pearson took out Andy Peers to put the home side ahead but wins for Garry Stephens and Matt Green got the Defending champs ahead only for Ryan Orchard to knock in 30 break as he beat Mark Ashton with Bob Stephens getting the better of Geoff Merriman in the last for the visitors victory.

Mevagissey B can count themselves unlucky to lose 4-1 at Bethel D losing 2 frames on the Black ball Mark Gregory got the visitors off to a good start beating Tyrone Stephens but wins for Steve Benallack Geoff Hawken Liam Jones and Jason Pascoe sealed the good home win

St Blazey A got a great 4-1 home win against Bugle B to stay top of the Rees league in what is looking to be a very tight championship race. Dave Rundle beat Billy Vigus in the opener to get the away point but wins for Liam Reynolds, Chris Brown who had a 32 break Mark Cockayne and Andrew Kitt sealed the deal for the Blazey boys

Terry Mills, Lee McKinstry and Rob Bunney put Gorran Haven 3 up at home to Tregonissey C then Lee Hobbs beat Steve Williams to get an away point with Warren Ball beating Kelly McMullen in the last to keep the home side in 3rd place

Bethel C took a 3 frame lead at Lerryn through Howard Brett Roger Smithson and Ben Stunell but the home side battled back to take the final 2 games with wins for Graham Hoskin and Les Shakespeare

32

