  ('St Blazey A extend lead at top of Rees League', 'st-blazey-a-extend-lead-at-top-of-rees-memorial-league', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Match Report - Week 7 - 2023-2024', 'Bugle A claimed A narrow win at home to Bethel D to stay top of the Victory league although there lead has been cut by a point.', 'St Blazey A took all 5 frames at home to Lerryn', 'They gained the first 3 frames of the evening through Keiran Pearce, Gary Spencer and a potting masterclass by Andrew Best with Tyrone Stephens and Steve Benallack pulling back the final 2 frames of the evening.

Bethel A lost the first frame at home to Pelynt as Paul Woodman beat Bob Stephens but comprehensive wins for Garry Stephens, Mark Ashton (44 break) Andrew Peers and Matt Green saw them record good win.

Mevagissey A picked up a great win at St Neot as Ben Prynns Black ball win again Ant Maddams and victories for Rob Blamey and James Tomlinson sealed the win with Darren Lock and Steve Courts replying.

St Blazey B are still waiting for there 1st win as they could only get 2 frames) from Mevagissey B with Gavin Dyche playing and winning twice with Matt Mills /Mark Gregory and Dave Kendall getting the home points.

St Blazey A took all 5 frames at home to Lerryn, Andrew Kitt, Chris Brown, Mark Cockayne and Billy Vigus all had big wins with Liam Reynolds needing his 39 break to see off Les Shakespeare.

Tregonissey B and Gorran Haven had 4 very close frames all going down to the Black ball with Treggy squeezing home by the odd frame to stay in 2nd spot in the Rees league. Terry Mills and Lee McKinstry had put the visitors 2 up but the home side recovered to win through Darren Roberts, Ryan Orchard and Mark Haworth.

Bethel C are struggling for form and lost at home to Bugle B by the odd frame. Colin and Dave Rundle put the visitors 2 up but Leigh Rosevear pulled a frame back beating Mike Williams on the black but Roy Bayliss beat James Smithson to get the win with Howard Brett beating Keith Moore in the final frame.

Bethel B got 4 good points on there travels at Mevagissey C where Richard Tamblins defeat of Terry Nicholls was the home sides only success as Darren Biggen, Craig Nicholls, Adey Dyche and Mike Haley won for the Bethel boys.

44

MARK ASHTON

BETHEL A

