  ('Besty and Bristow bang in the big breaks', 'besty-and-bristow-bang-in-the-big-breaks', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Match Report - Week 8 - 2023-2024', 'Both leaders of the Victory and Rees leagues dropped points this week allowing the second place teams to close in on the top spot', 'A special mention must be made for Josh Bristow who had a great 91 break against his teammate Gavin Dyche in the Bill Tom''s Competition', 'Victory leaders Bugle A were defeated for the first time this season despite Andrew Best knocking in a superb 90 break against Richard Broad to take the highest break prize so far. Len Flower levelled things up beating Keiran Pearce but Gary Spencer put Bugle back in front taking out Nigel Doble only for John Daniell and Andrew Gooch to get the next 2 frames against Justin Oxenham and Ian Powell respectively to seal a great win.

That slip up by the leaders gave Bethel A the chance to close the gap and they got all 5 frames at Mevagissey A which was harsh on the home side Garry Stephens beat Richard Lakeman on the Black to take the first then Andrew Peers got 3 snookers and a respotted black to beat an unlucky Ben Prynn a close win for Mark Ashton over Rob Blamey followed with Comfortable wins for Matt Green and Bob Stephens.

St Blazey B got there first win beating St Neot by the odd frame with Josh Bristows single point win over Steve Courts in the opener pivotal on the night. Gavin Dyche knocked in a 38 break as he dispatched Simon Oshea but Martin Richards horrid run of drawing the big guns continued as Darren Lock put him to the sword to bring the away side back into the game but Dayle Dyche beat Darren Oshea to seal the win before Ant Maddams hammered Clive Stuthridge in the finale.

Mevagissey B got 2 good points at Tregonissey A through Matt Mills and Nathan Shaw with Richard Pearson, Geoff Merriman and Jason Cocks getting the home points to sit joint 3rd in the table with there opponents.

St Blazey A dropping 2 points at Bethel B allowed Tregonissey B the chance to close the gap on them which they duly did getting all 5 frames against there C team now being 2 points behind the Blazey boys with a game in hand.

Liam Reynolds, Billy Vigus and Andrew Kitt got the leaders frames at Bethel B who replied through Mike Haley and Terry Nicholls Blackwall win over Stuart Dewings.

Mevagissey C recovered from losing the first 2 games at Bugle B to record a fantastic win over there much fancied opponents.

Dave Rundle and Keith Moore had put the home side in a good place but Oliver Watson Adrian Evans and Glyn Tamblin pulled out a great win and took the runabout shield home as well.

Bethel C moved up a place after a tight win at Gorran Haven as Ben Stunell Leigh Rosevear and Howard Brett all won with Lee McKinstry and Steve Williams successfully for the home side.

A special mention must be made for Josh Bristow who had a great 91 break against his teammate Gavin Dyche in the Bill Tom''s Competition.

90

ANDREW BEST

BUGLE A

VICTORY LEAGUE

38

GAVIN DYCHE

ST BLAZEY B

