  ('St Blazey A extend lead at the top of the rees', 'st-blazey-a-extend-lead-at-the-top-of-the-rees', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Match Report - Week 1 - 2023-2024', 'Mevagissey B got 4 excellent points at St Neot to move into 3rd place in the Victory League. Only Darren Lock who knocked in a 31 break against St Matt Rowe could register a home win as Matt Mills Ben Rothwell Mark Gregory and Nathan Shaw bought the bacon home for the seasiders.', 'Jason Cocks had breaks of 31 and 33 against Len Flower as Tregonissey A got a win at Pelynt', 'Mevagissey A had only Darren Powells (32 break) to show as he beat Steve Benallack as Bethel D came away with 4 frames with 3 frames closely contested but the run was with the away side who won through Liam Jones Geoff Hawken Jason Pascoe and Tyrone Stephens.

Jason Cocks had breaks of 31 and 33 against Len Flower as Tregonissey A got a win at Pelynt by the odd frame There was never more than a frame between them all night with Andrew Gooch and Nigel Doble won for the home side with Geoff Merriman and Richard Pearson got Treggys other 2 frames.

St Blazey A completed there 1st half of the season with a 4-1 home win over Mevagissey C who had Adrian Evans to thank for there point as he took out the big scalp of Liam Reynolds, But Mark Cockayne Billy Vigus Chris Brown (38 break) and Andrew Kitt all won to leave them 6 points clear at the top of the Rees league although Tregonissey B have 2 games in hand.

Terry Middleton and Les Shakespeare both won as Lerryn picked up 2 welcome points at Bugle B with Graham Hoskin unlucky to lose out to Dave Rundle on the Black in the final frame of the evening with Keith Moore and Colin Rundle having earlier won there frames for the home side.

