  ('New Teams Pairs Competition - Format', 'new-teams-pairs-competition-format', 'Competitions', '[]'::jsonb, 'Latest Committee Meeting News', 'New Teams Pairs Competition (4 frames)', null, 'Present: C Perring (president)G Stephens (chairman)G Hawken (Secretary)D Biggen Gary Spencer C Stuthridge M Green Mark Cockayne Rich Pearson (all committee) Apologies: K Moore (vice chairman)

This new format has two pairs per team.

Geoff Hawken has provided the following guidance.

Frame 1 pair 1 v pair 1 Frame 2 pair 2 v pair 2 Frame 3 pair 1 v pair 2 Frame 4 pair 2 v pair 1

All frames played until finished.

This competition isn''t handicapped.

If matches finish 2 - 2 then total team points scored determines winners.

St Blazey A have received a walk-over as Mevagissey A have withdrawn from the competition.

Please post a copy of the scorecard on facebook and also e-mail Geoff Hawken and Clive Stuthridge the result.

The Team Pairs Draw can be found here:', '2023-11-28', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Bethel A hit the top', 'bethel-a-hit-the-top', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Match Report - Week 9 - 2023-2024', 'Bugle A condemned Bethel A to there 1st defeat of the season on Tuesday night with wins for Jake Moore Gary Spencer and Andrew Best who knocked in a 39 break when beating Matt Green putting them 3 frames up but the visitors pulled back the last 2 frames through Bob Stephens and Garry Stephens who had a 47 break', 'Tregonissey B took 3 frames at Bethel B to move 3 points behind leaders St Blazey A', 'Mevagissey A got 2 good points at Tregonissey A with wins for Rich Lakeman and Darren Powell but victories for Jason Cocks Kevin Harris and Dan Allen saw the home side get the win

Steve Courts beat Steve Benallack on the Black to get St Neot off to a winning start at Bethel D and Darren Lock along with Darren Oshea got them the win moving them away from the bottom 2 with Jason Pascoe and Liam Jones getting the home points

St Blazey B need points and they started well at home to Pelynt taking the first 2 frames through Dayle Dyche and Andrew Kitt who stepped up from the A team to help out but the away side fought back to get the win as Andrew Gooch Nigel Doble and John Daniells Black ball win over Martin Richards sealed the result

On Wednesday Bethel A got all 5 frames at home to St Blazey B to jump to the top of the Victory league leading Bugle A by 3 points excellent wins for Matt Green over Liam Reynolds and Bob Stephens over Josh Bristow being the standout wins on the night

Tregonissey B took 3 frames at Bethel B to move 3 points behind leaders St Blazey A with a game play at Mevagissey C last night Kyle Bennetts Ryan Orchard and Mark Haworth took there frames with Mike Haley and Craig Nicholls replying

Bugle B move up to 3rd place in the Rees league after a good 4 1 win at Tregonissey C as both Mike Williams and Keith Moore won on the black with Dave Rundle and Nige Couchman also victorious with Lee Hobbs taking out Colin Rundle for the home point

Glyn Tamblin and Adrian Evans both won on the Black ball along with a win for Mark Ferguson saw Mevagissey C get a great win at home to Bethel C who had Leigh Rosevear and Howard Brett to thank for there points

