  ('Late finishes and drama', 'late-finishes-and-drama', 'Competitions', '[]'::jsonb, 'Team Handicap Quarter final results', 'There was a very late finish at Bethel as the A team overcame Bugle A by 3 frames to 1 in the team handicap 1/4 finals. Garry Stephens took the opener against Kieren Pearce but Gary Spencer levelled things to up beating and Andy Peers, Matt Green then won a big frame taking out Andrew Best and victory was secured as Bob Stephens beat Gary Moore.', 'Chris Perring nail-biting win over Geoff Merriman leaving the home side feeling absolutely gutted.', 'Bethel D joined there A team in the next draw after beating there B team taking the first 3 frames through Steve Benallack Geoff Hawken and Ross McMenemy

There was a real cliffhanger at Mevagissey B who sneaked past St Blazey B as captain Mark Gregory got the better of Clive Stuthridge in the deciding frame with all of the 1st 4 frames going down to the pink or black ball. Matt Rowe and Nathan Shaws great win over Josh Bristow got the other home wins with Gavin Dyche and Martin Richards getting the away frames.

St Neot sneaked past Tregonissey A winning on the Black in the final frame. Darren lock pulled back his big handicap deficit beating Dan Allen in the opener with Jason Cocks doing the same against Ant Maddams to level up Darren Oshea pipped Kevin Harris to put St Neot back in front but Rich Pearsons big win against Steve Courts leaving Chris Perring nail-biting win over Geoff Merriman leaving the home side feeling absolutely gutted.

St Blazey A progressed to the Handicap Plate semi finals after a 3 1 win at Bugle B with Mark Cockayne Andrew Kitt and Liam Reynolds close win over Keith Moore securing the visitors victory with Dave Rundle defeat of Stuart Dewings the home side only consolation

Bethel C switched there game to Lerryn due to table unavailability as lost out going down 3 frames to1 Graham Hoskin and David Vipond put the home side 2 up with Howard Brett pulling a frame back beating John Hancock but Terry Middleton low scoring win over Roger Smithson sealed the win

Pelynt move into the semi''s after winning the 1st 3 frames at Tregonissey C

John Daniell beat Lynn Kearns to get them moving then Len Flower just edged out Darren Elliott and Andrew Gooch pulled back a big handicap difference to beat Amanda Fleming to seal the win

In a rearranged Rees league game Tregonissey B came away from Mevagissey C with a 3 2 victory to sit level on points with St Blazey A at the halfway point of the season', '2023-12-18', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Bugle go back to the top of the Victory as St Blazey and Treg B stay locked at the top of the Rees', 'bugle-go-back-to-the-top-of-the-victory-as-st-blazey-and-treg-b-stay-locked-at-t', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Match Report - Week 11 - 2023-2024', 'With the Victory league leaders Bethel A having there bye week Bugle A went back to the top of the league after beating Mevagissey A by 4 frames to 1', 'Ben Rothwells Black ball win over John Daniell got Mevagissey B off to a good start at home to Pelynt', 'Justin Oxenham sneaked past Ben Prynn in the opener to get the home side off to a good start but Matt Chesterfield levelled things up beating Keiran Pearce but comfortable victories for Gary Spencer Andrew Best and Ian Powell confirmed the win

Ben Rothwells Black ball win over John Daniell got Mevagissey B off to a good start at home to Pelynt but Len Flower and Nigel Doble put the visitors ahead and it got better for the morning as Andrew Gooch beat Matt Mills on the Black and Richard Broad beat Matt Rowe to take their tally to 4 frames

St Blazey B got 3 frames at Bethel D to help their efforts to climb the ladder, Martin Richards, Clive Stuthridge and Josh Bristow were their Victors with Jason Pascoe and Geoff Hawken replying.

St Neot against Tregonissey A was postponed.

St Blazey A and Tregonissey B stay locked together at top of the Rees league after both won 3 2 Ben Stunell and Howard Brett''s great win against Liam Reynolds got Bethel C their points against the Blazey Boys with Andrew Kitt, Chris Brown and Mark Cockayne getting wins.

David Vipond and Graham Hoskin got 2 great points for Lerryn at Tregonissey B who had Kyle Bennetts Mark Haworth and Nathan Taylor to thank for the win.

Kelly McMullens Black ball win over Matt Moore was Tregonissey C''s only success at Bethel B as Craig and Terry Nicholls along with Mike Haley and Ady Dyche got the home points

Gorran Haven picked up a 3 2 win at Mevagissey C to move into 3rd place in the table addicted up the runabout in the process

