  ('St Blazey A and Bethel keep top spots in both leagues', 'st-blazey-a-and-bethel-keep-top-spots-in-both-leagues', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Match Report - Week 12 - 2023-2024', 'Bethel A went back to the top of the Victory league after a comprehensive 5 0 home win over Mevagissey B to sit a point clear of Bugle A with a game in hand', 'St Blazey A came away from Gorran Haven with 4 very good points', 'Andy Peers had a 30 break whilst beating Matt Rowe and big wins for Matt Green Mark Ashton Garry Stephens and Bob Stephens saw them hit the top.

Martin Richards and Josh Bristow got 2 frames for St Blazey B at home to Bugle A helping them in there effort to get away from the relegation zone with Justin Oxenham Andrew Best and Gary Spencer getting the away points.

Pelynt took 4 frames at home to St Neot to move up to 3rd place with Nigel Dobles Black ball win against Steve Courts the only real close game with Darren Lock beating Richard Broad to secure for the away point.

Dan Allen and Kevin Harris put Tregonissey A 2 up at home to Bethel D who fought back to level through Steve Benallack and Jason Pascoe but a potting masterclass by Jason Cocks against Liam Jones secured the home sides win.

St Blazey A came away from Gorran Haven with 4 very good points with Mark Cockayne inflicting a first defeat of the season on Lee McKinstry there were also victories for Liam Reynolds Stuart Dewings and still unbeaten Chris Brown with Steve Williams beating Andrew Kitt to stop the whitewash.

Bugle B knocked Tregonissey B title hopes after a good odd frame win with wins for Dave Rundle Roy Bayliss and Keith Moore with Mark Haworth and Kyle Bennetts getting the away points leaving them 2 behind the blazey boys.

Darren Elliott put Tregonissey C ahead against his old side Mevagissey C but Adrian Evans equalised beating Amanda Fleming then 2 black ball wins for Glyn Tamblin and Mark Ferguson got meva the win with Lee Hobbs beating Rich Tamblin in the nights final frame.

Les Shakespeare and Graham Hoskin won 2 close frames to put Lerryn in a good place at home to Bethel B but good wins for Ady Dyche, Craig Nicholls and Matt Moore turned the game around for a win for the visitors

