  ('Massive shock at the top of the Rees League', 'massive-shock-at-the-top-of-the-rees-league', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Match Report - Week 13 - 2023-2024', 'A massive shock at the top of the Rees league saw Bethel C whitewash second place Tregonissey B', 'St Blazey A got all 5 frames against a plucky Tregonissey C team by large margins and are surely now hot favourites for the title.', 'Allowing St Blazey A to open up a 7 point lead on the treggy boys going into last nights game between the 2 Wins for Leigh Rosevear, Paul and James Smithson and Ben Stunells Black ball win over Darren Roberts gives the Bethel boys an outside chance of getting the runners up spot.

Elsewhere in the league Bethel B moved into 3rd place after a fine win at home to Bugle B Dave and Colin Rundle had put the visitors 2 1 up sandwiched between Matt Moores win over Mike Williams but Terry Nicholls and Ady Dyche took the final 2 frames for the win.

St Blazey A got all 5 frames against a plucky Tregonissey C team by large margins and are surely now hot favourites for the title.

Another good night for Bethel A at the top of the Victory league getting 4 frames at St Neot Matt Green knocked in breaks of 31 and 37 against Darren Oshea with Garry Stephens getting a fine 51 break as he took out Steve Courts with other wins for Andy Peers and Mark Ashton although Darren Lock beat Bob Stephens in the final frame having a 41 break against Bob Stephens.

Bugle A slipped up at home to Tregonissey A losing by the odd frame and relinquished the runabout shield Andrew Best took the 1st frame and Gary Spencer the last having a 40 break but wins for Kevin Harris Richard Pearson and Jason Cocks saw the treggy boys prevail.

Pelynt got the third 4 1 win on the trot to move into 3rd place after beating Bethel D away Andrew Gooch beat Steve Benallack on the pink and Nigel Doble beat Liam Jones on the Black along win wins for John Daniell and Len Flower with Geoff Hawken taking out Richard Broad to save the whitewash.

