  ('Bethel A increase lead at the top', 'bethel-a-increase-lead-at-the-top', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Match Report - Week 15 - 2023-2024', 'Bethel A got 4 good points at home to Tregonissey A to increase there lead at the top of the Victory league. Geoff Merriman got the visitors off to a good start beating Andy Peers but big wins for Mark Ashton and Matt Green put Bethel ahead and the last 2 frames were very tight but went the way of Garry and Bob Stephens to leave them sitting pretty with 4 matches to play', 'Bethel C still have an outside chance of promotion and picked up 3 points at home to Lerryn as James Smithson Howard Brett and Ben Stunell all won with Graham Hoskin and James Stephens replying', 'Steve Courts and Darren Lock put St Neot 2 up after home to Bugle A but the game turned right around as Andrew Best Jake Moore and Gary Spencer all won moving the Bugle boys back into second place in the league.

Mevagissey B will feel hard done by after a 4 1 home defeat to Bethel D losing out on 3 of the 4 black ball finishes on the night Liam Jones, Steve Benallack Jason Pascoe and Geoff Hawken all won for the away side with Matt Mills beating Ross McMenemy to get the solitary home point.

It''s pretty much same as you were in the Rees league as the top 2 both got odd frame wins Liam Reynolds put St Blazey A ahead at Bugle B taking out Mike Williams with Keith Moore levelling up after beating Stuart Dewings, Mark Cockayne hammered Dave Rundle to put the blazey back in front but Colin Rundle got a great win over Chris Brown leaving Billy Vigus to take a tight game against Gary Stocks to seal the win leaving them 10 points clear with 3 games to play.

Tregonissey B stay 2nd after beating a plucky Mevagissey C team who got there 2 frames through Richard Tamblin and Adrian Evans with Ryan Orchard who knocked in a 35 break, Mark Craddock and Darren Roberts getting the home frames.

Bethel C still have an outside chance of promotion and picked up 3 points at home to Lerryn as James Smithson, Howard Brett and Ben Stunell all won with Graham Hoskin and James Stephens replying.

Gorran Haven also still have a sniff on the runners up spot and took the first 2 frames at Tregonissey C through Warren Ball and Lee McKinstry but the home side responded as Lee Hobbs and Darren Elliott drew them level but Terry Mills took the last frame against Kelly McMullen to get the win.

35

RYAN ORCHARD

