  ('Committee Meeting 29-01-2024', 'committee-meeting-29-01-2024', 'League Meetings', '[]'::jsonb, 'Latest Committee Meeting News', 'St Blazey and District snooker league - Committee meeting held at Bethel social club on Monday 29th January 2024', null, 'Present: Garry Stephens (chairman) Keith Moore (vice chairman) Geoff Hawken (secretary) Richard Pearson (website) Darren Biggen, Clive Stuthridge, Gary Spencer, Matt Green, Mark Cockayne (Committee) Apologies: Chris Perring (president)

Chairman opened meeting and thanked everyone for their attendance. Secretary read out the minutes of the last meeting which were agreed as true.

1. Secretary had made contact with Tim Johnson secretary of the Godolphin League regarding playing the interleague match in early April and he was going to take that suggestion to his Committee.
2. Nigel Doble is keen to introduce an interleague match with the Liskeard League and would be getting in touch with the secretary after speaking to there Committee A new trophy would be purchased with both leagues paying half each of the cost.

1. Presentation night is on Easter Saturday 30th March at Bethel Club 19.30hrs start with a cost of £5 a person including a pasty.
2. Entertainment is by The Strutts Band.
3. Anyone wishing to donate a raffle prize please contact the secretary.
4. Boynton trophy will be played on Saturday 16th march at Bethel Club.
5. All players will pay £5 on the day to play and will be drawn out a player.
6. If there player win the trophy they will receive 50% of the money paid.
7. Runner up wins 30% and the 2 losing semi finalists 10%.
8. 8 teams had purchased the new league shirts so far with Tregonissey B soon to order there''s.
9. Competition entries were £90 up this season.

1. Some players are still not sending results to Clive which will be passed on to the AGM and put on the website.
2. A couple of players have been given far too high handicaps but as they signed up after the committee had set everyone''s handicaps these cannot be altered until next season.
3. Many people have been commenting on the 5 point rule for the away player in some competition''s. This has been the case for a very long time but it was agreed by those Present to take to the AGM for discussion.
4. When teams cancel a match they need to tell the secretary of the date of the rearranged fixture so the website can be set up to take the result.
5. There had been a lot of discussion about using 2 tables at venues to quicken up the evening after discussion it was agreed that if a player does not want to play on the 2nd table that is there right so can decline the offer.
6. Proposal by Gary Spencer to hold a 2 day competition for maximum of 24 players on the weekend of the World championship final 4 groups of 6 players who all play each player in there group so playing 5 frames on day 1. The top 2 players from each group would qualify to play in the finals day comp with players 3rd and 4th going into the plate competition on finals day Gary was then asked to submit a full brief to by shared to captains for there feedback.
7. There had been reports of some very slow play by some players so the committee would like to remind everyone that the referee has it in his powers to ask a player to speed there game up.
8. There had been a lot of walkovers given in the competitions this year which is disappointing especially as a lot of clubs pay there entry fee and we will discuss the matter at the AGM.
9. Proposal by Richard Pearson that when we do the draws of a competitions 1st round next season the following rounds will all be set up on the website but will not be shown until the previous round has been completed. (eg 1 draw at the start and results follow on automatically and are NOT drawn round by round. This will make it a lot easier for Richard Clive and Mark and save them having to manually put the new draws on each time and was supported by all present.
10. Players are also reminded that there should be no more practice after 19.15 thus allowing time for tables to be prepared for the 19.30hrs start.
11. There being no further business the chairman closed the meeting at 21.15 hrs.', '2024-01-31', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Bugle A suffer damaging defeat to leave there chances of runners up spot in the balance', 'bugle-a-suffer-damaging-defeat-to-leave-there-chances-of-runners-up-spot-in-the-', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Match Report - Week 16 - 2023-2024', 'Pelynt kept up there great run of form as they beat champions elect Bethel A by 3 frames to 2 to enhance there own chances of getting the runners up spot', 'Mevagissey A got a much needed victory at home to St Neot leaving there opponents looking over there shoulders at the relegation zone', 'Steve Courts and Darren Lock put St Neot 2 up after home to Bugle A but the game turned right around as Andrew Best Jake Moore and Gary Spencer all won moving the Bugle boys back into second place in the league.

Mevagissey B will feel hard done by after a 4 1 home defeat to Bethel D losing out on 3 of the 4 black ball finishes on the night Liam Jones, Steve Benallack Jason Pascoe and Geoff Hawken all won for the away side with Matt Mills beating Ross McMenemy to get the solitary home point..

Garry Stephens beat Nigel Doble in the opener to put Bethel ahead but wins for Len Flower Andrew Gooch who knocked in breaks of 40 and 30 against Mark Ashton and Richard Broad put them 3 1 up but Bob Stephens sneaked past John Daniell in the last pulling a frame back.

Bugle A suffered a damaging 4 1 defeat at Bethel D to leave there chances of runners up spot in the balance with there next game at home to Pelynt. Gary Spencer got them off to a good start beating Geoff Hawken but Steve Benallack potted well to beat Kieren Pearce then Jason Pascoe''s superb blue to black clearance saw him beat Jake Moore then Justin Oxenham was very unlucky to lose out to Geoff Hawken who was playing his 1 extra game a season on the Black and a no show by there 5th player gave Ross McMenemy a walkover.

Mevagissey A got a much needed victory at home to St Neot leaving there opponents looking over there shoulders at the relegation zone. Darren Powell and Ben Prynn put them 2 up but Darren Lock and Steve Courts pulled the visitors level only for James Tomlinson to see off Chris Perring to claim the win.

St Blazey B are rallying hard to avoid the drop and got 3 points at home to Mevagissey B Gavin Dyche took the opener but Matt Rowe and Nathan Shaw put meva ahead only for Josh Bristow Black ball defeat of Mark Gregory and Clive Stuthridge ''s win against Ben Rothwell completing the evening.

St Blazey A all but secured promotion with a 3 2 win at Lerryn and only need 2 points from there remaining 2 games to be crowned champions. Wins for Stuart Dewings Andrew Kitt and Chris Brown got the win with Terry Middleton and James Stephens replying.

Tregonissey B got a great 4 1 win at Gorran Haven and look good for the runners up spot. Lee McKinstry got the home side off to a good start beating Mark Haworth but Ryan Orchard Kyle Bennetts Darren Roberts and Nathan Taylor all chalked up big wins for the visitors Mark Ferguson unluckily went in off the Black in the final frame to gift Darren Biggen and Bethel B victory against Mevagissey C by the odd frame.

Ben Baker and a great brown to pink clearance by Adrian Evans got Meva''s points with Craig Nicholls and Ady Dyche getting the other home wins.

League sponsor James Smithson got Bethel C off to a good start at Bugle B by beating Mike Williams but Keith Moore levelled things up beating Ben Stunell Howard Brett put the visitors back in front cruising past Colin Rundle but Mark Stuthridge making a rare appearance beat Roger Smithson on the Black leaving Dave Rundle to get his teams win by beating Leigh Rosevear.

40

ANDREW GOOCH

