  ('Team handicap matches - latest results', 'team-handicap-matches-latest-results', 'Competitions', '[]'::jsonb, 'Match Report - Week 1 - 2023-2024', 'Mevagissey B defeated St Neot by 3 frames to 1 to reach the team handicap final for a second year running Matt Rowe got them off to a good start beating Nick Collins but Darren Lock levelled things up knocking in a break of 67 whilst beating Ben Rothwell Nathan Shaw then had a big win over Chris Perring to put the Meva boys back in front with Dave Kendall getting the better of Steve Courts to seal the win.', 'Mevagissey A got a much needed victory at home to St Neot leaving there opponents looking over there shoulders at the relegation zone', 'In the final they will play Bethel D who beat there in A team by 3 frames to nil.

Geoff Hawken sneaked past Mark Ashton in a scrappy first frame followed by an excellent win for Steve Benallack over Matt Green and the win was confirmed as Liam Jones had a big win over Andy Peers.

.

In the Team Plate handicap there were 2 really close semi finals both going down to the wire Lerryn went 2 up at home to St Blazey A as John Hancock and James Stephens took out Mark Cockayne and Billy Vigus respectively Liam Reynolds got 1 back beating Graham Hoskin on the Black with Chris Brown pulling Blazey level getting the better of Dave Vipond on the Black.

It looked very good for the home side as Terry Middleton was 23 points ahead of Stuart Dewings with only Green upwards left but Stuart made a 25 clearance break to seal a great win.

Kyle Bennetts beat Len Flower to put Tregonissey B ahead against Pelynt with Nigel Doble beating Nathan Taylor to level up then Mark Haworth beat a very out of sorts Andrew Gooch to put the treggy boys ahead again only for Richard Broad to beat Darren Roberts on the Black leaving John Daniell to sneak past Ryan Orchard in a very tight and low scoring final frame to take the match.

In a rearranged Victory league game Mevagissey A gave themselves a better chance of avoiding relegation as they beat 2nd bottom St Blazey B by the odd frame. Dayle Dyche had a 31 break beating Matt Chesterfield in the opener with James Tomlinson levelling things up taking out Gavin Dyche then Clive Stuthridge beat Rich Lakeman to put the blazey boys back in the lead but good victories for Ben Prynn over Martin Richards and Darren Powell over Josh Bristow got the meva boys a welcome win.

67

