VICTORY LEAGUE', '2024-02-23', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('St Blazey A clinch the Rees league title', 'st-blazey-a-clinch-the-rees-league-title', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Match Report - Week 1 - 2023-2024', 'Pelynt kept up there great run of form as they beat champions elect Bethel A by 3 frames to 2 to enhance there own chances of getting the runners up spot', 'Andrew Best put the hosts back in front knocking in a fine 61 break against Richard Broad', 'Bethel A only need a point from there final 2 games to retain the Victory league title after a 3-2 home win over Mevagissey A who appear destined to drop into the Rees league.

Gary Stephens, Matt Green and Mark Ashton got the home points with Rich Lakeman and Ben Prynn both playing very well to register the away points.

Pelynt will be delighted to of come away from Bugle A with 2 points in the race for the runners up spot leaving them only a single point behind there opponents but with a game more to play.

Justin Oxenham beat Nigel Doble on the Black to get Bugle off to good start but Andrew Gooch had a 33 break to level up but Andrew Best put the hosts back in front knocking in a fine 61 break against Richard Broad, but parity was restored with Len Flower having a 32 when beating Keiran Pearce leaving Gary Spencer to see off John Daniell to get a much needed win.

Dave Kendall put Mevagissey B ahead at home to Tregonissey A but Rich Pearson Kevin Harris and Jason Cocks took the next 3 games to get a win for the visitors with Matt Mills beating Dan Allen for Meva''s other point.

St Neot all but relegated St Blazey B opening up a 4 point gap on there opponents with 2 games to play by getting 4 frames at home to them. Steve Courts got there 1st frame beating Dayle Dyche but Clive Stuthridge responded getting the better of Ian Hawke but Darren Lock knocked in a 52 break as he despatched Martin Richards with further wins for Chris Perring and Anthony Maddams making it a good night for the home side.

St Blazey A clinched the Rees league title as they raced into a 3 frame lead at home to Bethel B through Chris Brown, Liam Reynolds who had a 42 break and Billy Vigus but Craig Nicholls narrowly beat Stuart Dewings and Ady Dyches respotted Black ball win over Mark Cockayne pulled a couple back for the away side.

Tregonissey B all but secured the runners up spot after beating there own C team by the odd frame Lee Hobbs avenged his semi final defeat in the Willie Thomas competition by beating Ryan Orchard to put the C team ahead but Darren Roberts and Kyle Bennetts both won to sneak ahead before Jamie Hobbs levelled up as he beat Nathan Taylor leaving Mark Haworth to beat Amanda Fleming to seal the win.

James and Roger Smithson both won to put Bethel C 2 up at home to Gorran Haven who responded with Terry Mills, Warren Ball and Lee McKinstry who trailed Martin Powell for all of the game before potting the Black to win and seal a great comeback for the visitors.

Bugle B jumped up to joint 3rd as they got a good win at Mevagissey C. Adrian Evans had put the hosts ahead beating Colin Rundle but big wins for Roy Bayliss, Keith Moore, Dave Rundle and Mike Williams took the points back to the clay Country.

61

ANDREW BEST

