Related News', '2024-02-28', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Bethel A retain Victory League title', 'bethel-a-retain-victory-league-title', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Match Report - Week 15 - 2023-2024', 'The Victory league winners and the 2 relegation places were confirmed on Tuesday night with 1 week of the season left to play', 'St Blazey A completed there season winning all but 1 game after getting all 5 frames at Mevagissey', 'Bethel A retained the title with a win at St Blazey B which Sent there opponents into the Rees league for next season.

Gavin Dyche took the opener against Bob Stephens but that was as good as it got for the home side as Andy Peers Garry Stephens Mark Ashton and Matt Green all won easily to seal the win.

Pelynt moved into the Runners up spot picking up 2 frames at Tregonissey A and are a single point ahead of Bugle A going into last nights final games. Jason Cocks, Rich Pearson and Kevin Harris had put the treggy boys 3 up but Richard Broad and Andrew Gooch managed to win the final 2 frames to give them a great chance of claiming some silverware.

Mevagissey A were relegated but got a good win at Bethel D as Ben Prynn Darren Powell and Rich Lakeman all won with Liam Jones and Jason Pascoe replying.

St Neot confirmed there place in the top division beating Mevagissey B by the odd frame Chris Perring took the 1st frame against Matt Rowe but Dave Kendall and Ben Rothwell got the next 2 putting the Meva boys ahead but Darren Lock and Steve Courts easily got the final 2 frames for the win.

St Blazey A completed there season winning all but 1 game after getting all 5 frames at Mevagissey C through Mark Cockayne, Liam Reynolds, Stuart Dewings, Billy Vigus and a extra game for Mark Cockayne showing the ruthless streak which has been evident all season.

Bethel C moved to within point''s of Tregonissey B in the runners up spot as they beat Tregonissey C by 4 frames to 1 leaving a nervous night for a few in last nights final games Ben Stunell was the only 1 to miss out as Darren Elliott put him to the sword with Roger and James Smithson along with Leigh Rosevear and Howard Brett claiming the away win.

Warren Ball of Gorran Haven was unaware of the snooker report each week but he will certainly be reading it in the future especially getting his side off to a good start beating Darren Biggen of Bethel B Steve Williams and Terry Mills also secured wins with Ady Dyche beating the team dangerous Lee McKinstry and Matt Moore taking out Rob Bunney for the home side.

Bugle B went 3 up away at Lerryn courtesy of Roy Bayliss and Colin and Dave Rundle but the home side fought back to take the final 2 frames as James Stephens beat Mike Williams and John Hancock took out Keith Moore In the first league final to be played newcomers Kyle Bennetts and Nathan Taylor of Tregonissey B took the Doubles Handicap title with a 3 nil win over a strangely out of sorts Ben Prynn and Matt Chesterfield of Mevagissey A who just couldn''t find any sign of form all night with their opponents taking the Important balls when the opportunities arose.

Bethel A won the new Team Handicap competition on Thursday night beating Bugle A by 3 frames to 1 at Tregonissey club. Matt Green and Mark Ashton won both of there games by large scores with Andy Peers and Garry Stephens winning 1of there games to make it a league and Cup double for the team

And in the country over 65s final on Thursday night played at Mevagissey 82 year old John Daniell of Pelynt came back from 2 down to beat Bob Stephens of Bethel after taking the next 4 frames to be a worthy winner of the competition.', '2024-03-05', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Pelynt and Treg B grab runners-up spots', 'pelynt-and-treg-b-grab-runners-up-spots', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Match Report - Week 16 - 2023-2024', 'Pelynt knew that they would get the runners up spot in the Victory League as long as they matched or beat Bugle A''s result in the final league games of the season and they did this as both sides suffered 3 2 defeats', 'Mevagissey A got a much needed victory at home to St Neot leaving there opponents looking over there shoulders at the relegation zone', 'Josh Bristow put St Blazey B ahead at Pelynt beating Len Flower but Andrew Gooch levelled things up taking out Martin Richards and won the Victory rankings trophy in the process then Clive Stuthridge and Gavin Dyche both won to give the visitors the win with Richard Broad taking the final frame to claim the silverware for the hosts.

Garry Stephens beat Jake Moore to put Bethel A ahead at home to Bugle A with Kieren Pearce levelling things up beating Andy Peers but Mark Ashton and Bob Stephens excellent win over Andrew Best sealed the win with Gary Spencers win over Matt Green concluding the evening.

Relegated Mevagissey A did there best trying to hold on to the runabout shield by taking the first 2 frames at home to Tregonissey A with wins for James Tomlinson and Ben Prynn but the visitors pulled off a great comeback to win thanks to Geoff Merriman, Jason Cocks (30 break)and Rich Pearson.

St Neot finished with a 4-1 home win over Bethel D helped by winning 2 of the 3 Black ball games on the night Ant Maddams Darren Lock, Steve Courts and Nigel Collins were all winners with Liam Jones getting the solitary away point.

Tregonissey B claimed the runners up spot in the Rees league getting all 5 frames at home to Bethel B Ryan Orchard and Mark Craddock won the first 2 frames in close finishes with Nathan Taylor, Darren Roberts and Kyle Bennetts all having comfortable wins.

Amanda Fleming and Darren Elliott got 2 good points for Tregonissey C at Bugle B who replied through Roy Bayliss and Colin and Dave Rundle.

Lerryn got a good win at Gorran Haven by the odd frame as Les Shakespeare James Stephens with the prized scalp of Lee McKinstry and Darwin Fitz all won with Terry Mills and Steve Williams getting the home points.

Mevagissey C got a great win at Bethel C with wins for Benjamin Baker, Richard Tamblin and Adrian Evans with Howard Brett and Ben Stunell taking the home frames.

30

JASON COCKS

TREGONISSEY A

