  ('Liskeard League all-stars beat St Blazey and District snooker league all stars 8-6', 'liskeard-league-all-stars-beat-st-blazey-and-district-snooker-league-all-stars-8', 'League News', '[]'::jsonb, 'At St Neot on Friday 12th April 19.00hrs start', 'On Friday 12th April in a close fought match Liskeard all stars pipped St Blazey all stars 8-6 to take the title', null, null, '2024-04-02', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Gordon Boynton Trophy - Recap', 'gordon-boynton-trophy-recap', 'Competitions', '[]'::jsonb, '27 players made the early 10am start at Bethel social club to compete in the Boynton Trophy with the normal 1 frame shootout played off people''s handicap', '27 players made the early 10am start at Bethel social club to compete in the Boynton Trophy with the normal 1 frame shootout played off people''s handicap.', null, 'There were the normal early shocks with some big names like Darren Lock Gary Spencer Andrew Gooch all going out.

The first semi final saw Garry Stephens pull back a 53 point deficit to beat Kyle Bennetts on the Black with Geoff Hawken pipping Chris Brown again on the Black to move into the finalin which Garry carried on like he had all day playing a very solid game to become a deserved winner of the trophy.

Photo Gallery Below under draw', '2024-04-03', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('St Blazey & District Snooker Presentation evening -  Recap', 'st-blazey-district-snooker-presentation-evening-recap', 'League News', '[]'::jsonb, 'Photo Gallery', null, null, null, '2024-04-05', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Committee Meeting 11-07-2024', 'committee-meeting-11-07-2024', 'League Meetings', '[]'::jsonb, 'Latest Committee Meeting News', 'St Blazey and District snooker league - Committee meeting held at Bethel social club on TUESDAY 11th July 2024', null, 'Present: G Stephens (chairman)K Moore (vice chairman)C Perring (President) G Hawken (secretary)C Stuthridge D Biggen M Green G Spencer (Committee) Apologies: R Pearson M Cockayne (website)

Chairman opened meeting and thanked everyone for their attendance. Secretary read the minutes of the last meeting and were agreed as a true record

1. Secretary told the meeting that the Godolphin League had showed no interest in playing the interleague match so the Chairman was going to approach the mining league to see if they wanted to play a yearly game against the St Blazey League He would also ask for the shield to be returned by the Godolphin League to possibly use verses the Mining league
2. The interleague match against the Liskeard League was played at St Neot on Friday 12th April and resulted in a 8 to 6 win for the Liskeard League. Everyone really enjoyed the evening and it was agreed to ask Nigel Doble to play at St Neot every year with it being such a good venue
3. Presentation night was as always a good night with the raffle again being well supported but in future we will be asking people attending to pay there entry money via the league bank account as it is hard on the night to keep account of who has paid what and also people not showing up as promised is costing the league money We will explain this to all at the AGM
4. The Boynton trophy was again a good day and the £5 side bet to have a player being "sponsored" was a great success
5. There was then a discussion about the 5 point rule in some competitions for the away player It was felt that comp entries would suffer if this was removed so we would keep it the same unless a proposal to change this was put to the AGM to be discussed and voted on
6. The secretary was getting a lot of negative feedback regarding just doing 1 draw for the competitions with each round being revealed after the previous round had been completed as it would be very easy to work out who is playing who next and we would be discussing this with Rich Pearson and Mark Cockayne before the AGM
7. AGM is on Tuesday 16th July 2024 at Bethel social club 19.30hrs start
8. Season to start on Tuesday 24th September 2024
9. Presentation night is on Saturday 5th April 2024
10. Entertainment TBC

1. Chris Perring felt that having a Rees league singles competition would be well supported and all agreed so that will come into operation next season
2. The secretary would remind captains that any player can refuse to play on table number 2 if they want to play on the main match table
3. Any new player that was not given a handicap by the committee when all handicaps are assessed will be given a handicap by the committee after they have played 2 matches
4. Justin Oxenham and Ryan Orchard will be joining the committee at the AGM
5. The Committee felt that 3 real positives from last season were the new 4 player rule saving cancellations The new 4 a side Team pairs competition was very well supported and Chris Perring praised how the website was working a lot better and thanked our website team There being no further business the chairman closed the meeting at 20.30hrs', '2024-06-15', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Annual General Meeting 2024 (AGM)', 'annual-general-meeting-2024-agm', 'League Meetings', '[]'::jsonb, 'St Blazey and District snooker league AGM was held at Bethel social club on Tuesday 16th July 2024', 'St Blazey and District snooker league AGM was held at Bethel social club on Tuesday 16th July 2024', null, 'Present: Chris Perring President, Garry Stephens Chairman Keith Moore Vice President Geoff Hawken Secretary Richard Pearson Clive Stuthridge Mark Cockayne Darren Biggen Gary Spencer Matt Green all committee John Daniell Andrew Gooch Terry Nicholls Craig Nicholls Ryan Orchard Andrew Best Justin Oxenham Jason Pascoe Adrian Evans Mark Gregory John Hancock Terry Middleton. Apologies: Steve Courts Ian Ball Lee McKinstry

Chairman opened the meeting and thanked everyone for their attendance. Minutes of the 2022/23 season were read and agreed as a true record.

1. A new Victory league winners trophy and a new Team Pairs trophy had been purchased and we are now waiting for St Blazey to get a new trophy cabinet to retire the old cups to along with future trophies as they are replaced
2. Victory League winners beat the Rest of the league by 3 frames to nil
3. Rees League winners St Blazey A lost to Rest of the league by 3 frames to 1
4. Online banking was working well with lots of clubs and players paying for competitions and league shirts online
5. The Rees league runabout shield would start the season at Mevagissey C after a draw took place prior to the meeting
6. 8 teams had purchased the new league shirts
7. All the players were happy to pay £5 at the Boynton trophy to *buy/sponsor a player with the winner getting 50% the runner up 30% and the losing semi finalists getting 10% each so this will continue every year
8. Rule sheets for next season would be the same as no new proposals had been received Scorecards were given out to clubs at the meeting and the Secretary would deliver the new handicap sheet and fixtures as soon as possible also competitions sheets which will show a new Rees league singles competition which the committee had agreed to run
9. Secretary said how pleased the league was that Chris Perring was now President and a great asset to the league
10. Lerryn proposal to play with 4 players was a great rule to bring in as very few games were postponed and the new Team pairs competition with 4 players a side attracted 14 teams up from 5 teams the season before
11. Any new player who hasn''t got a handicap will be assessed after his first 2 games and given a handicap
12. Secretary then thanked everyone who had helped him during the season and thanked the committee for all they do and time given up to the league

1. Balance as at 30/06/2022 £1607.05
2. Balance as at 15/07 /2024 £1796.26
3. Surplus on year £ 189.21
4. Secretary explained that the cost of the trophies had risen steeply also we paid for 2 new ones and a half share for the new Interleague trophy to be played against the Liskeard League but said that he had already spoken to Lex Dezigns about the prices of engraving the trophies for next season which had to be reduced or else we would look at alternative options
5. Richard Pearson stated that he would buy the website server a different way next season to save money
6. Secretary said no honorarium had been paid out this year as he would like a discussion at the next committee meeting to see how the website money should be distributed between Richard Mark and Clive
7. After a brief discussion Mark Cockayne proposed the balance sheet be approved Seconded by Richard Pearson and was carried unanimously

1. After a good discussion it was decided that the Boynton trophy would be the last trophy to be played for every year as it would give the secretary a chance to select a more accurate list of players to play in the tournament and we would also put the presentation night back a couple of weeks as the finals were crammed in ever season
2. Dates for next season
3. Shootout at St Blazey on Tuesday 17th September
4. 1st league games are on Tuesday 24th September
5. As normal weeks have been set aside for team handicap and team pairs games
6. Boynton trophy will be on Saturday 5th April 2025
7. Presentation night TBC
8. Nigel Doble put forward a suggestion for players to pick there own player to buy/sponsor at the Boynton trophy but as some players don''t turn up until late because they are drawn late to play it was decided to do the draw as normal
9. Election of officers and committee all elected on block
10. Justin Oxenham and Ryan Orchard have joined the committee

There being no further business the chairman closed the meeting at 20.15hrs', '2024-07-19', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Snooker Shoot-Out Handicap Competition', 'snooker-shoot-out-handicap-competition', 'Competitions', '[]'::jsonb, '2024', null, null, 'Tuesday 20th September at St Blazey Football Club (19.00 hrs start) more 1 frame shoot-out 10 second shot clock through frame 10 minute frame Played off 50% of players league handicap Prize breakdown Winner 40% Runner-up 20% Losing semi-finalists 10% Highest-break 20% Can captains please let their team-mates know about this competition Limited to the first 32 players, £2 entry fee Please contact your Team Captain to register', '2024-09-14', true, 'Richard Pearson'),
  ('Shock defeat for defending Victory champions', 'shock-defeat-for-defending-victory-champions', 'Match Reports', '[]'::jsonb, 'Defending champions Bethel A were beaten by Mevagissey B in the seasons  opener in a shock start to there league campaign.', 'Defending champions Bethel A were beaten by Mevagissey B in the seasons opener in a shock start to there league campaign.', 'Relegated Mevagissey A got off to a great start beating Bethel B by 4 frames to 1', 'The sea-siders took the first 3 frames through Pete Chambers Ben Rothwell and Nathan Shaw with Matt Green and Mark Ashton pulling back the final 2 frames for the home side.

Last year''s runners up Pelynt made a strong start beating Bethel D by 4 frames to 1 Paul Woodman beat Geoff Hawken in the opener with Jason Pascoe pipping Len Flower to level up Andrew Gooch squeezed past Ross McMenemy to regain the lead with Jamie Daniell edging out Paul Baron and Richard Broad played beautifully to defeat Steve Benallack.

2 black ball wins for Andrew Best and Keiran Pearce put Bugle A ahead at promoted St Blazey A and comfortably victories for Justin Oxenham new boy Josh Bristow and Gary Spencer who knock in a 36 break saw them as early leaders in the Victory League.

A black ball win for Jason Cocks over Ryan Orchard got Tregonissey A off to a good start at home to here B side further wins for Geoff Merriman Ryan Bilson and John Bates secured there 4 points with Kyle Bennetts beating Kevin Harris for his sides point.

In the Rees league Gorran Haven made a strong start by taking all 5 frames against Lerryn Rob Bunney Matt Fox making a rare appearance Steve Williams Newcomer Dan Pascoe and Lee McKinstry surprisingly not on holiday took all there games to start with a bang.

Relagated St Blazey B got a good 4 1 win at Bugle B taking 4 frames through Clive Stuthridge George Taylor Martin Richards and Gavin Dyche with Mike Williams winning the last frame against Kev Masters.

Relegated Mevagissey A got off to a great start beating Bethel B by 4 frames to 1 with Ady Dyche beating Charlie Prynn in the last frame of the night to stop the whitewash after Rich Lakeman Darren Powell Ben Prynn and Matt Chesterfield took the first 4 games.

Bethel C v Mevagissey C was a long night with the home side getting a 3 2 win with Benjamin Baker and Adrian Evans scoring for the away side but Howard Brett James Smithson and dad Roger Smithson got the home side over the line.

36

GARY SPENCER

BUGLE A

